#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:801
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/ITEMS.txt.py:803
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A wheel of prized unicorn's-milk frelandeau cheese. Sliced onto crackers, it"
" is the perfect compliment to a snifter of fine tobersk brandy."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:802
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/ITEMS.txt.py:804
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A log of Vori eldenbrie cheese. Though many have tried to duplicate its "
"subtle, smoky flavor, only the master Frost Giant cheese masters of the "
"frozen Vori wastes know the secrets of its formulation."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:803
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/ITEMS.txt.py:805
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A ball of dunduck cheese. Made in small batches by the goblins of Erathia, "
"most consider it an acquired taste."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:804
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:3
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Crude Longsword"
msgstr "Espada larga rudimentaria"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:804
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:3
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Though notched and dented, this longsword is still an effective weapon."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:805
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:4
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Elven Saber"
msgstr "Sable élfico"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:805
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:4
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Saber"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:805
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:4
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A common elven weapon, this saber is a deadly, if unremarkable, weapon."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:806
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:5
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Keen Longsword"
msgstr "Espada larga afilada"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:806
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:5
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Although this longsword appears quite old, the edge of the blade is "
"unusually sharp.  It was quite probably enchanted to remain that way during "
"its creation."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:807
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:6
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Graceful Sword"
msgstr "Espada grácil"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:807
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A high quality longsword, monogrammed initials near the base of the pommel "
"indicate it was forged by master weaponsmith Mekorig the Blind circa "
"780-800."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:808
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:7
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Duelist Blade"
msgstr "Hoja del duelista"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:808
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:7
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"These rare blades were forged sometime before the Silence, and have been "
"used by noble duelists who want to die in style for centuries.  No two are "
"quite alike, but all share bloody histories."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:809
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:8
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This simple two-handed sword with a leather grip is a common design in "
"Erathia."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:810
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:9
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:10
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Great Sword"
msgstr "Espada grande"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:810
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:9
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"An effective, deadly design employed by less well disciplined armies "
"throughout time.  The smith of this particular two-handed sword thoughtfully"
" added a blood groove down the center of the blade."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:811
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:10
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:11
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Heroic Sword"
msgstr "Espada heroica"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:811
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:10
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"It is thought by some master swordsmen that a wavy blade is a bit stronger "
"than a straight one, and does more damage when it strikes an opponent.  That"
" may or may not be true, but one thing is certain--this particular sword's "
"craftsmanship is amongst the finest you've ever seen."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:812
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:11
msgctxt "items"
msgid "A polished broadsword commonly used by all forces in Erathia."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:813
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:12
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:13
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Steel Broadsword"
msgstr "Espada ancha de acero"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:813
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:12
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:13
msgctxt "items"
msgid "A fine Erathian steel broadsword of excellent quality and edge."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:814
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Master Broadsword"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:814
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:13
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"More a falchion than a broadsword, this magnificent weapon retains a keen "
"edge in spite of its age."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:815
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:14
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The swept-back style of the cutlass helps opponents underestimate the "
"weapon's true reach.  Many unexperienced swordsmen have lost their lives to "
"this deceptive design."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:816
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:15
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Goblin Cutlass"
msgstr "Alfanje goblin"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:816
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:15
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A strange mix of brass and some other, reddish metal provide this weapon "
"with its strange color and unusual strength.  Goblin craftsman are typically"
" unconcerned with appearance, but when it comes to killing, they can be "
"counted on to get it right.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:817
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Exquisite Cutlass"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:817
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:16
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:17
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Cleverly concealed initials near the pommel of this cutlass prove this "
"beautiful weapon to be the work of Alec Teling, master smith to Hareck IX, "
"Lord of Regna, and emperor of the Endless Ocean."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:818
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Improvised Dagger"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:818
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:17
msgctxt "items"
msgid "A crude dagger found in the hands of thieves and ruffians everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:819
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:18
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Dwarven Dagger"
msgstr "Daga enana"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:819
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:18
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"More like a short sword to a dwarf, this dagger is an excellent example of "
"superior dwarven engineering and inferior artistic creativity."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:820
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:19
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Sharktooth Dagger"
msgstr "Daga de diente de tiburón"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:820
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:19
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The 'blade' of this dagger is really a sharks' tooth taken from the waters "
"of the Quiet Ocean and mounted on a fancy handle.  It is very sharp and "
"light."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:821
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:20
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Assassin's Dagger"
msgstr "Daga del asesino"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:821
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:20
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The crosspiece of this dagger folds in to make concealment easier.  A spring"
" in the pommel snaps the crosspiece out very quietly when the dagger is "
"drawn from its sheath."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:822
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Wonder Dagger"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:822
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:21
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A weapon from the Time of Wonders, it is no longer possible to achieve a "
"sharper or stronger edge."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:823
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Shoddy Long Dagger"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:823
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:22
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The long dagger combines the extra reach of the sword with the stealth of "
"the dagger."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:824
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:23
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Erathian Long Dagger"
msgstr "Daga larga erathiana"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:824
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This long dagger is outwardly reminescent of the smaller Erathian daggers "
"made using shark teeth, but its edge is unmistakably steel. The construction"
" is sturdy and reliable and the blade is every bit as deadly as the shark "
"tooth -- except it holds an edge better and is easier to resharpen."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:825
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:24
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Exquisite Long Dagger"
msgstr "Daga larga exquisita"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:825
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:24
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The spare, yet appealing design of this long dagger is typical of pre-"
"Silence artifacts.  This particular style was very popular at the time, but "
"since more than a thousand years have passed, few remain.  Like everything "
"from the time of the Silence, it looks as new as the day it was made."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:826
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:25
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Crude Axe"
msgstr "Hacha rudimentaria"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:826
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:25
msgctxt "items"
msgid "This primitive axe is more like a simple tool than a weapon."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:827
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:26
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:27
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Battle Axe"
msgstr "Hacha de batalla"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:827
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:26
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The flared edge of the blade is a common style used by low budget human "
"armies and bandits."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:828
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:27
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:29
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Dwarven Axe"
msgstr "Hacha enana"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:828
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:27
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Typical Dwarven manufacture:  Strong, practical, and plain."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:829
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:28
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Steel Axe"
msgstr "Hacha de acero"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:829
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:28
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"One of several crates full of such axes stolen from the Dwarves by the "
"Warlocks of Nighon.  Each of these weapons has been tempered and enchanted "
"by the Stone City foundry, and stamped with their mark."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:830
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:29
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Minotaur Axe"
msgstr "Hacha de minotauro"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:830
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:29
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Double bladed axes like these are powerfully enchanted by Minotaur sorcerers"
" in a secret process known only to them.  These axes are light where they "
"should be heavy, and slice through metal armor as easily as they slice "
"through cloth."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:831
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:30
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Poleaxe"
msgstr "Hacha de asta"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:831
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:30
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This style of long hafted axe has better reach and more power than the "
"normal one-handed axe."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:832
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:31
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Warrior's Poleaxe"
msgstr "Hacha de asta del guerrero"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:832
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:31
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This poleaxe has a sharper blade equipped with all the latest in military "
"technology:  Blood grooves, whistle-holes, and a counterbalanced, smaller "
"blade behind the haft for tricky, disembowling, backstrokes."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:833
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:32
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Headsman's Poleaxe"
msgstr "Hacha de asta del verdugo"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:833
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:32
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"So named for the execution device favored by headsmen, the Headsman's "
"Poleaxe sports a longer blade to reduce messy and embarassing execution "
"mistakes.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:834
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:33
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Crude Spear"
msgstr "Lanza rudimentaria"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:834
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:33
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Though constructed with a head of sharpened rock lashed to a rough stick, "
"this spear can cause serious damage. (+1D9 if used two-handed)."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:835
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:34
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Soldier's spear"
msgstr "Lanza del Soldado"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:835
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:34
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Spears like this are found in all armies where their versatility as both "
"pole and melee weapons are demonstrated regulary."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:836
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:35
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Elven Spear"
msgstr "Lanza élfica"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:836
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:35
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Elven weapons are almost always as graceful as they are practical.  The "
"spear's style and elegance have not come at the expense of practical "
"qualities such as the sturdy attachement of head to haft, nor the choices of"
" metal and haft grip."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:837
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:36
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Cruel Spear"
msgstr "Lanza cruel"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:837
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:36
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The triangular shape of the spear head leads to especially painful wounds "
"that do not heal easily or well.  Runic enchantments inscribed along the "
"haft suggest enchantments that enhance the cruel effect of the triangular "
"head."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:838
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:37
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Sublime Spear"
msgstr "Lanza sublime"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:838
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:37
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A smithy symbol and date stamp indicate this spear was made in the magical "
"forges of Governor Padish 12 years before the Silence."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:839
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Old Halberd"
msgstr "Alabarda vieja"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:839
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:38
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Like all Halberds, this weapon is basically an axe with a very long haft.  "
"It's a versatile weapon--doubling as a spear when fighting room is tight, or"
" a staff when personal defense is needed.  This one is of ordinary "
"worksmanship and materials."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:840
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:39
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Weighted Halberd"
msgstr "Alabarda contrapesada"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:840
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:39
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The haft of this halberd has been cored, and filled with a lead rod.  When "
"the weapon is swung, the lead rod slides to the blade end of the halberd "
"with a loud crack, adding force and weight to the blow."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:841
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:40
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Mighty Halberd"
msgstr "Alabarda poderosa"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:841
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:40
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A small stamp on the blade of this weapon indicates it was constructed in "
"the famous Mekorig Foundry by the master himself, Mekorig the Blind.  You "
"would be hard pressed to find a finer Halberd anywhere in the world "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:842
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Crude Trident"
msgstr "Tridente rudimentario"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:842
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:41
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A variant of the farmer's pitchfork, the trident had been used by spear "
"fishermen since time began.  Now it is the traditional weapon of sea-going "
"warriors throughout the world."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:843
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:42
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Barbed Trident"
msgstr "Tridente con púas"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:843
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:42
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Improving on the basic trident design, the tips of the tines have rough, "
"backwards facing barbs.  This designs causes much more damage as the weapon "
"is pulled from the victim."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:844
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:43
msgctxt "items"
msgid "War Trident"
msgstr "Tridente de Guerra"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:844
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:43
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A style favored by the Imerial Regnan Navy, the two side tines of the war "
"trident are thin and sharp to make slashing as easy as stabbing.  To further"
" impress enemies, the tines are gilded in brass, and the haft painted "
"yellow, giving the appearance that the Regnans are fighting with golden "
"weapons."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:845
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:44
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Crude Bow"
msgstr "Arco rudimentario"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:845 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:846 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:847 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:848 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:849 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1645 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1646 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1647 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1648 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1649
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:44
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:45
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:46
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:47
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:48
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:45
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:46
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:47
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:48
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:49
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Longbow"
msgstr "Arco largo"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:845 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1645
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:44
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:45
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A simple longbow constructed of common materials and uninspired design."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:846
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:45
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A higher quality long bow designed after the elven long bow, but without the"
" elven skill."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:847
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:46
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Elven Longbow"
msgstr "Arco largo élfico"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:847
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:46
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Etched initials at the base of the bow indicate this bow was made by master "
"bowyer Ivan Selving's workshop during the Timber Wars of the late 600's."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:848
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:47
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Composite Bow"
msgstr "Arco compuesto"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:848
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:47
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Composite bows are made of a variety of materials and pieces, instead of a "
"single piece of wood.  They are generally more flexible and powerful than "
"regular bows."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:849
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:48
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Griffin Bow"
msgstr "Arco del grifo"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:849
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:48
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The grisly materials used in this bow--a griffin's skull and tough spine--"
"make for a surprisingly tough and powerful bow.  Needless to say, the "
"materials are hard to harvest, and griffins fight back much harder than Yew "
"trees."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:850
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Crude Crossbow"
msgstr "Ballesta rudimentaria"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:850
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:49
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Although crossbows have many advantages--locking string catches, superior "
"shot strength, easy to learn--they don't compare to the longbow when speed "
"and range are critical.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:851
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:50
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Heavy Crossbow"
msgstr "Ballesta pesada"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:851
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:50
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:51
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"These crossbows were stockpiled by Archibald just prior to the Succession "
"War for use against his brother.  As with most decisions involving death, "
"Archibald chose wisely.  These crossbows are amongst the best in the land."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:852
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:51
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Ideal Crossbow"
msgstr "Ballesta ideal"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:852
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This is as much a crossbow as it is a work of art -- a sculpture of a dark "
"figure with curved horns for bowstaves. It would be less surprising if it "
"were indeed just a decoration, but it has all the mechanical parts it needs,"
" cleverly worked into the wooden frame. Its origins are unknown, though it "
"is safe to assume it's a product of dark sorcery, and its performance "
"matches its appearance."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:853
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Crude Mace"
msgstr "Maza rudimentaria"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:853
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:52
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Barely more sophisticated than a normal club, the mace is slightly more "
"effective and much more durable."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:854
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:53
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Spiked Mace"
msgstr "Maza con pinchos"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:854
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:53
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This weapon is designed to inflict good damage to both armored and unarmored"
" opponents."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:855
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:54
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Zealot Mace"
msgstr "Maza del Fanático"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:855
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:54
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A common mace from Karigor, it displays the same superior quality of all "
"weapons and equipment from that island."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:856
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:55
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Dwarven Morningstar"
msgstr "Lucero del alba enano"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:856
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:55
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A variation of the mace, the morningstar hits slower but much harder.  The "
"spikes on the ball guarantee recipients will feel the blow, regardless of "
"armor or hide."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:857
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:56
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Supreme Flail"
msgstr "Mangual supremo"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:857
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:56
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A heavier, more menacing weapon than a morningstar, flails are almost as "
"dangerous to their wielder as they are to opponents.  Flails like this one "
"are of the highest quality, thoroughly enchanted by the Warlock Guild of "
"Nighon."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:858
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Makeshift Hammer"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:858
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:57
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A crude, tool-like weapon, this hammer includes a wrist chain to prevent it "
"from dropping from your hand."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:859
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Battle Hammer"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:859
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This relatively simple hammer's greatest advantages are its low striking "
"area due to the size of the head, and the spike on the reverse which could "
"be used to inflict rather nasty wounds."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:860
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:59
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Dwarven Hammer"
msgstr "Martillo enano"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:860
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:59
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The top of the line for the hammer family of weapons.  This Dwarven hammer "
"was constructed in the forges of Stone City, and every feature is perfect--"
"balance, weight, handle material, head construction--all the best possible "
"with modern metalurgical techniques."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:861
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Primitive Club"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:861
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:60
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A primitive weapon usable by even the stupidest of monsters.  This club is "
"constructed of Erathian oak."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:862
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Thorned Club"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:862
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This small club has been fitted with sharp, thorn-like spikes that somewhat "
"make up for its compact size."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:863
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Steel Club"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:863
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:62
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The symmetry and length of the knob at the end of the club is the only "
"feature that distinguishes this club from a mace.  The balance is good, the "
"construction is solid, but it IS still a club, and you can't expect that "
"much from it.  Probably of Goblin manufacture."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:864
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Simple Staff"
msgstr "Bastón sencillo"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:864
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:63
msgctxt "items"
msgid "The staff is the common weapon of the oppressed."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:865
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:64
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Iron Core Staff"
msgstr "Bastón con núcleo de hierro"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:865
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:64
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This staff has been filled with iron to give a harder punch than an ordinary"
" staff, while appearing to be nothing more than a fancy walking stick.  The "
"wood is polished Ash, carved with a tasteful design."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:866
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:65
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Wizard Staff"
msgstr "Bastón de Mago"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:866
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:65
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A weird combination of wood, glass and aluminum form the staff, while a "
"crystalline skull tops it.  The whole weapon is bound together with glue and"
" strong enchantments to make one of the lightest, strongest staves in the "
"world."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:867 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1667
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:66
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:67
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Blaster"
msgstr "Bláster"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:867 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:868 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1667 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1668
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:66
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:67
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:67
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:68
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Ancient Weapon"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:867
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:66
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A weapon of awesome power, almost certainly created during the Time of "
"Wonders."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:868 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1668
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:67
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:68
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Blaster Rifle"
msgstr "Rifle bláster"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:868
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:67
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The finest of personal weapons made during the Time of Wonders, Blaster "
"Rifles can deal death faster than any weapon you have ever seen."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:869
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Crude Leather Armor"
msgstr "Armadura de cuero burda"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:869
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:68
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Leather armor is the lightest and most easily worn armor, but it offers less"
" protection that the heavier armors.  The leather in this suit was "
"improperly cured and still stinks of the chemicals used in its production."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:870
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:69
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:70
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Studded Leather"
msgstr "Cuero tachonado"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:870
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:69
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This suit of leather armor is held together with bronze studs instead of "
"leather straps.  This construction makes it a bit stronger, but also a bit "
"heavier."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:871
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:70
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Officer's Leather"
msgstr "Armadura de cuero del oficial"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:871
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:70
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:71
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"An otherwise ordinary suit of leather armor, this suit is imbued with a "
"subtle enchantment that strengthens the material against blows without "
"increasing weight."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:872
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Light Dragon Leather"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:872
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:71
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:72
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Standard issue leather armor for officers in the Regnan Navy.  All such "
"leather armor receives enchantments to strengthen and lighten it during its "
"creation in the Regnan Armories."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:873
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:72
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Royal Leather"
msgstr "Cuero real"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:873
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:72
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Only a few suits like this one have been made, and all were special orders "
"for members of the royal family of Erathia--the Gryphonhearts.  This one had"
" to come from one of three places:  Stolen from the palace armory, taken on "
"the battlefield, or robbed from a grave."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:874
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Disheveled Chain Mail"
msgstr "Cota de malla maltrecha"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:874 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:875 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:876 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:877 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:878 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1674 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1675 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1676 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1677 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1678
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:73
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:74
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:75
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:76
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:77
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:535
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:74
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:75
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:76
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:77
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:78
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Chain Mail"
msgstr "Cota de malla"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:874
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:73
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Chain mail is an armor formed of small, interlocking loops of metal.  It "
"looks like someone forgot to oil the rings, or maybe left it out in the rain"
" because rust has begun to form in the armpits and under the collars."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:875
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Quality Steel Chain Mail"
msgstr "Cota de malla de acero de calidad"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:875
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:74
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This suit of chain mail is made of steel and is actually lighter than "
"similar suits made of plain iron.  Thin rings were used in its construction,"
" but the steel composition makes them very strong."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:876
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:75
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Fine Chain Mail"
msgstr "Cota de malla fina"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:876
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:75
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Very high quality steel is reinforced with fine studded leather to soften "
"blows while minimizing weight.  The leather portions are quite artistic and "
"pleasing to the eye."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:877
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:76
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Resplendent Chain Mail"
msgstr "Cota de malla resplandeciente"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:877
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:76
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A distinctive suit of armor meant to aid recognition of officers during "
"battle.  Besides just looking good, the armor is amongst the lightest, most "
"supple chain mail available.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:878
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:77
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Golden Chain Mail"
msgstr "Cota de malla dorada"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:878
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:77
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A very rare suit of armor turned out by the Heavenly Forges of Governor "
"Padish before the Silence.  The armor was originally worn strictly by the "
"Governor's highest military officers as a badge of office.  It is not just "
"for show; this chain mail is lighter, stronger, and more supple than any "
"other chain in the world."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:879
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:78
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Plate armor is the strongest armor available.  It is much heavier than other"
" suits of armor, and requires considerable practice to get used to wearing."
"  This suit is made of iron, and the workmanship is unremarkable."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:880
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:79
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Splendid Plate Armor"
msgstr "Armadura de placas espléndida"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:880
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:79
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Forged in an Erathian armory, this suit of plate armor bears a recent stamp:"
"  B.R., Steadwick Foundry, 1151.  The initials are those of Byron "
"Rockermann, Royal armorsmith of Erathia.  His work is competent and elegant."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:881
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:80
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Noble Plate Armor"
msgstr "Armadura de placas de noble"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:881
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:80
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A suit of armor so fine could only have come from the forge of the Master "
"himself--Mekorig the Blind.  Indeed, this one bears the initials of his son,"
" Kasev Mekorig near the heel.  The joints move easily, and the metal has a "
"curious triple plated construction that makes it thin and light, yet "
"incredibly strong.  Padding in comfortable, too."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:882
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:81
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Goblin Shield"
msgstr "Escudo goblin"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:882
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:81
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A simple, old shield with crude markings on its face.  Ugly, but practical."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:883
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:82
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:87
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Wooden Shield"
msgstr "Escudo de madera"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:883
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:82
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This shield is made of wood framed by iron.  It is heavy, but well "
"constructed and in good condition."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:884
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:83
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Horseman's Shield"
msgstr "Escudo del jinete"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:884
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:83
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Narrow and tapered at the bottom, this shield is intended for battle on "
"horseback, but will work just fine on foot.  Construction is tight and "
"materials are tough--it should be able to resist a direct spear thrust."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:885
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:84
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Sterling Shield"
msgstr "Escudo excepcional"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:885 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1685
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:84
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:85
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Made of a lightweight metal, this shield has a foundry stamp from the "
"Kelebrim armory.  Though light, the material is very strong, and the metal "
"is welded almost seamlessly.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:886
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:85
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Phynaxian Shield"
msgstr "Escudo phynaxiano"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:886
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:85
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:86
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"These shields were forged by the Phynaxian empire during its brief rise to "
"power on the steppes of southern Erathia (790-864).  They are made of stalt,"
" a metal that takes well to enchantment, and contributed heavily to "
"Phynaxian military might.  Unfortunately, very little of the metal could be "
"mined, and Phynaxia fell in 864 A.S. to an Elvish offensive."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:887
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Crude Buckler"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:887
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:86
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A small wood buckler designed to protect against arrows without encumbering "
"its wielder.  The quality is amaturish, but it's in good condition and will "
"serve its purpose."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:888
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:87
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:88
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Bronze Shield"
msgstr "Escudo de bronce"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:888
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Bronze shields are lighter than iron shields of the same size, but aren't "
"nearly as strong. This particular one is of a slightly larger variety and "
"has been reasonably well protected from rusting."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:889
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:88
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Metal Shield"
msgstr "Escudo de metal"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:889
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:88
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The pretty red design on the surface of this shield means it's from Deyja, "
"and the paint isn't paint.  Emulsifiers and preservatives help to retain the"
" original color…"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:890
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:89
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Alloyed Shield"
msgstr "Escudo de aleación"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:890
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:89
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The exact mixture of metals in these strong shields has been lost for "
"hundreds of years.  Attempts to rediscover the process used to make them "
"have been miserable failures.  There is absolutely nothing enchanted or "
"magical about these shields--any enchantment they carry was added after they"
" were created.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:891
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:90
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Majestic Shield"
msgstr "Escudo majestuoso"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:891
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:90
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The dark, golden color of these shields is actually a flaw.  About fifty of "
"these shields were turned out by the Heavenly Forge as it began to fail.  "
"Although imperfect, they are second only to shields built by the Forge in "
"its prime."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:892
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:91
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Horned Helm"
msgstr "Yelmo con cuernos"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:892
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:91
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This cheap helm is better suited for a costume party than a battle.  The "
"horns have been glued onto a rigid leather cap dyed black to make it look "
"scarier.  The material is brittle and flaky, and will probably come apart at"
" just the wrong time."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:893
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:92
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Conscript's Helm"
msgstr "Yelmo del recluta"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:893
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:92
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The simple style and uniformity of these helms is meant to strike terror "
"into the hearts of enemies when they see row upon row of bronze, spiked "
"helms marching toward them.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:894
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Elven Helm"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:894
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:93
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:94
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This helm design has been used by the Elves of Erathia since before the "
"Silence.  It is composed of silver and steel and is very strong."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:895
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:94
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Phynaxian Helm"
msgstr "Yelmo phynaxiano"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:895
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:94
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Worn by Phynaxian Dragoons during the expansion of their empire a few "
"hundred years ago, these helms are tough, flexible, and light.  They are "
"made of two strips of dragonhide bound together with stalt metal studs."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:896
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:95
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Mogred Helm"
msgstr "Yelmo de Mogred"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:896
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:95
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Half made from the skull of the ferocious Mogred beast in Karigor, these "
"helms grow more uncommon every year as the Mogreds approach extinction.  Two"
" poisonous spines used to grow from the red spots on the front of the helm."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:897
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:96
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Peasant Hat"
msgstr "Sombrero de campesino"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:897
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:96
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A common, cloth hat with a feather stuck in the band to add a dash of style."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:898
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:97
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Traveller's Hat"
msgstr "Sombrero de viajero"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:898
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:97
msgctxt "items"
msgid "A simple hat meant to keep sun and dust off a traveller's head."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:899
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:98
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:98
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Fancy Hat"
msgstr "Sombrero elegante"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:899
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:98
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The latest in fashion, this hat harkens back to more of a working class "
"style.  It isn't really the hat that's in style, it's the working man that "
"young nobles are trying to emulate--who in turn seeks to emulate the "
"nobleman…"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:900 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:901 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:902 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1700 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1701 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1702
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/ITEMS.txt.py:524
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:99
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:100
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:101
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:100
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:101
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:102
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Crown"
msgstr "Corona"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:900
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:99
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This is a cheap crown of the sort that primitive goblins wear to mock human "
"customs.  The metal is bronze, and the gem is made of glass."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:901
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:100
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Noble Crown"
msgstr "Corona noble"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:901
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A fine, if somewhat ostentatious crown made with gold leaf and large, high "
"quality amethysts.  It suits nobles of your station well."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:902
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Royal Crown"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:902
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Crowns such as this are what you might find adorning the heads of genuine "
"royalty. Not only do they look elegant without being gaudy, but they're "
"perfectly suited to taking the strongest of enchantments."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:903
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/ITEMS.txt.py:120
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:102
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:103
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Leather Belt"
msgstr "Cinturón de cuero"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:903
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:102
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A peasant's belt.  This one is made of poorly cured leather and rusting iron"
" studs."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:904
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:103
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Fine Belt"
msgstr "Cinturón fino"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:904
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:103
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A well crafted belt of well tanned leather and fine stitching.  The buckle "
"is made of polished silver."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:905
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:104
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Strong Belt"
msgstr "Cinturón fuerte"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:905
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:104
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A tough, yet high quality leather belt.  This one was probably made in "
"western Erathia.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:906
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:105
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Silver Belt"
msgstr "Cinturón de plata"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:906
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:105
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A very nicely made silver belt, this one is old, but well cared for.  "
"There's no trace of tarnish on any of the links--just a bit of wear around "
"the buckle."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:907
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:106
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Gilded Belt"
msgstr "Cinturón chapado en oro"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:907
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Gaudy to an extreme, this belt is made of solid 14-karat gold.  Each link "
"has a different, low quality image stamped on its face.  Tasteless, but "
"valuable."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:908
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Fine Leather Cloak"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:908
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:107
msgctxt "items"
msgid "A simple traveller's cloak."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:909
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:108
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Huntsman's Cloak"
msgstr "Capa del cazador"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:909
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:108
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A huntsman's cloak colored green to make the wearer difficult to see in the "
"forest.  Not much to look at, but it serves its purpose."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:910
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:109
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Ranger's Cloak"
msgstr "Capa del explorador"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:910
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Woven from plant fibers found in the Tularean Forest, these cloaks are the "
"traditional garb of the Elven Rangers. This black variety is reserved for "
"higher ranking Rangers and symbolizes their status as leaders."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:911
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:110
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Elegant Cloak"
msgstr "Capa elegante"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:911
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:110
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This cloak is of the quality preferred by wealthy nobles and royalty.  It is"
" hard to find better."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:912
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:111
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Glorious Cloak"
msgstr "Capa Gloriosa"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:912
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:111
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Almost all cloaks like this one come with some sort of enchantment.  The "
"Warlocks of Nighon employ legions of mentally enslaved people to perform the"
" tedious weaving and ritual spell casting necessary to make these cloaks."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:913
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Pinched Gauntlets"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:913
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:112
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Low quality iron gauntlets with cloth linings to prevent blisters.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:914
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:113
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This pair of gauntlets is made of steel and decorated with brass tracery "
"along the outside of the palm and back of the hand.  It is in good repair "
"and well oiled."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:915
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:114
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Silver Mesh Gauntlets"
msgstr "Guanteletes de malla de plata"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:915
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:114
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A marvelous achievement, these gauntlets were forged and woven by the "
"Dwarves of Stone City.  The offer both flexibility and strong protection.  "
"The only trouble is that the wearer's skin is sometimes caught in the mesh, "
"leading to painful pinches."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:916
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:115
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Dragon Hide Gauntlets"
msgstr "Guanteletes de piel de dragón"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:916
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Dragon hide -- as can be expected -- makes for an outstanding material for "
"gauntlets, offering hand protection surpassing many simpler iron or steel "
"designs. The only downside is that the leather is thick and rigid, somewhat "
"limiting the dexterity of movements."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:917
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:116
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Mogred Gauntlets"
msgstr "Guanteletes de Mogred"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:917
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:116
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Made from the hide of the Mogred beast on Karigor, these gauntlets are "
"tough, supple, and magic resistant.  The two red spots used to have "
"poisonous spines growing from them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:918
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:117
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:118
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Leather Boots"
msgstr "Botas de cuero"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:918
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:117
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"These boots are made of soft leather for a more comfortable fit, but they "
"offer little protection in combat."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:919
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:118
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Steel Plated Boots"
msgstr "Botas con placas de acero"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:919
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:118
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This pair of leather boots has been fitted with steel plates on the top of "
"the foot and at the shin."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:920
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:119
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Ranger Boots"
msgstr "Botas de explorador"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:920
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:119
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A quality set of Erathian leather boots.  This pair has the usual features "
"of Erathian leather craftsmanship:  Soft, water resistant, and quiet.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:921
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:120
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Knight's Boots"
msgstr "Botas del caballero"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:921 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:1721
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:120
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:121
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Polished silver boots with velvet interiors, these boots are lighter than "
"steel boots and far more comfortable.  They look pretty snappy, too."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:922
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:121
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Paladin Boots"
msgstr "Botas de paladín"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:922
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:121
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Made in the forge of Byron Rockermann, these silver and steel boots are "
"amongst the best in the world.  The are enormously strong, yet fit "
"comfortable and flexibly in all the right spots."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:923
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:122
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Brass Ring"
msgstr "Anillo de latón"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:923
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:122
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A tarnished brass ring.  Polished up, you might be able to sell it for "
"something…but don't expect much."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:924
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:123
msgctxt "items"
msgid "A large, imperfect pearl adorns this otherwise unremarkable gold ring."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:925
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:124
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Platinum Ring"
msgstr "Anillo de platino"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:925
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:124
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"At first glance silver, this ring is actually made of platinum.  The "
"gemstone is a small, flawed diamond."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:926
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:125
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Emerald Ring"
msgstr "Anillo de esmeralda"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:926
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:125
msgctxt "items"
msgid "A large, cut emerald adorns an otherwise plain silver ring."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:927
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:126
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Sapphire Ring"
msgstr "Anillo de zafiro"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:927
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:126
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Three small sapphires are mounted at the top of this silver and gold ring.  "
"Rings of this quality are often enchanted."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:928
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:127
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Warlock's Ring"
msgstr "Anillo del brujo"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:928
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This complex and gaudy arrangement of amethysts on platinum can be "
"appealing, if you like that sort of thing."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:929
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:128
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Enchanted Ring"
msgstr "Anillo encantado"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:929
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:128
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A rare gem-within-gem of emerald and garnet is set upon a fine gold ring."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:930
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:129
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Dazzling Ring"
msgstr "Anillo deslumbrante"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:930
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:129
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A beautiful rosetta of rubies and emeralds on gold backing.  The ring itself"
" is platinum."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:931
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:130
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Wizard Ring"
msgstr "Anillo de Mago"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:931
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:130
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Three perfect garnets set into silver belie the enchantments used to create "
"this ring.  Handling the ring for long makes your hand tingle."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:932
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:131
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Angel's Ring"
msgstr "Anillo del Ángel"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:932
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:131
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A very strange brown stone (petrified wood?) is mounted on a metal that "
"looks like gold, but is much lighter."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:933
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:132
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Eyeball Amulet"
msgstr "Amuleto del globo ocular"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:933
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:132
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"This strange amulet has a glass eye on the end of a cheap brass chain.  A "
"novelty, but probably not worth much."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:934
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:133
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Bronze Amulet"
msgstr "Amuleto de bronce"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:934
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:133
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A baroque bronze amulet with an ill define image stamped on the face.  "
"Cheap, and tasteless."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:935
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:134
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Witch's Amulet"
msgstr "Amuleto de la bruja"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:935
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:134
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A plaster cast of a baby's hand was used to form this strange silver amulet."
"  There is some unidentifiable symbol stamped in the center of the amulet."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:936
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:135
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Death's Head Pendant"
msgstr "Colgante de calavera"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:936
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:135
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Straight out of Deyja, this is just the sort of thing you would expect from "
"Necromancers.  The silver skull in the center is modeled from a real, "
"shrunken skull, and the tiny rubies in the eyes glow in the dark."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:937
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:136
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Sun Amulet"
msgstr "Amuleto del Sol"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:937
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:136
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A glorious gold amulet with the ancient symbol of the sun in the center.  "
"The amulet is from Karigor, and the craftsmanship is flawless."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:938
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:137
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Wand of Fire"
msgstr "Varita del Fuego"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:938 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:939 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:940 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:941 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:942
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:137
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:138
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:139
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:140
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:141
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"The magical process that was used to enchant this wand turned it sky blue.  "
"It's made of wood and glass.  To use this wand, you must equip it as though "
"you were equipping a weapon."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:939
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:138
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Wand of Sparks"
msgstr "Varita de las Chispas"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:940
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:139
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Wand of Poison"
msgstr "Varita del Veneno"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:941
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:140
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:141
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Wand of Stunning"
msgstr "Varita de aturdimiento"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:942
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:141
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Wand of Harm"
msgstr "Varita de Dañar"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:943
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:142
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Fairy Wand of Light"
msgstr "Varita de Luz feérica"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:943 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:944 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:945 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:946 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:947
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:142
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:143
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:144
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:145
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:146
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A wooden wand painted green and banded with brass.  The wand is capped with "
"a large, flawed emerald.  To use this wand, you must equip it as though you "
"were equipping a weapon."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:944
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:143
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Fairy Wand of Ice"
msgstr "Varita feérica de Hielo"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:945
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:144
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Fairy Wand of Lashing"
msgstr "Varita feérica de latigazos"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:946
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:145
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:146
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Fairy Wand of Mind"
msgstr "Varita feérica de la Mente"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:947
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:146
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Fairy Wand of Swarms"
msgstr "Varita de Enjambres feérica"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:948
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:147
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:148
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Alacorn Wand of Fireballs"
msgstr "Varita Alacorn de bolas de fuego"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:948 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:949 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:950 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:951 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:952
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:147
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:148
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:149
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:150
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:151
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Made from the hollowed out horn of a unicorn and capped with a spiked brass "
"ball, wands like these are born of cruelty and evil.  The enchantment it "
"holds is useful;  the only real question is whether you believe your cause "
"justifies the use of an item so wickedly created.  To use this wand, you "
"must equip it as though you were equipping a weapon."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:949
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:148
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Alacorn Wand of Acid"
msgstr "Varita de alicornio del Ácido"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_ItemsTxt.txt.py:950
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/ITEMS.TXT.py:149
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Alacorn Wand of Lightning"
msgstr "Varita Alacorn del Relámpago"

