#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:2
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you see this text tell James."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:3
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:3
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If the pirates make it through our warriors we are certainly doomed!  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:4
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:4
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Our thanks for defeating the pirates!  Now if you could only do something "
"about the mountain of fire!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:5
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:5
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There is no way back to the village of Blood Drop!  I have no way of knowing"
" if my family lives or not!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:6
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:6
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You came through the Portals of Stone?  They are working?  We can return to "
"our families!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:7
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:7
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Argh!  Either get in the fight, or get out of our way!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:8
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:8
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Someone should clear out the caves that the dire wolves use for their lair."
"  If we had one less thing to worry about, things might get a little better!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:9
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:9
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I have heard rumors that the end of the world is near.  One look at that "
"crystal in the center of town, and I am tempted to believe them!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:10
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:10
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There was a pack of those vile wererats behind my house again last night.  "
"Someone should do something about the vile little creatures. Between those "
"vermin and the dire wolves it amazing that our children are safe!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:11
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:11
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Please don't hurt us!  Arion Hunter says we are friends now!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:12
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:12
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"We will be forever in your debt!  You have saved Ravenshore and all of "
"Jadame!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:13
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:13
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Would you like to fire the cannons in defense of Dagger Wound Island?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:14
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:14
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Help us!  If we do not push the pirates off the island all will be lost!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:15
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:15
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"With the Pirate Outpost defeated our homes are once again safe!  Thank you!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:16
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:16
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Ogres have become more of a problem in our daily lives.  If someone were to "
"deal with the Ogres in their fortress, maybe things would get better!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:17
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:17
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Warrior Wasps have built a large nest southeast of here.  They could become "
"a threat to the city if the nest grows too large."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:18
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:18
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"News from the different regions of Jadame has been very slow in getting to "
"Alvar.  I wonder if the merchants know what is going on in the world?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:19
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:19
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The sea of fire has destroyed our village!  Who knows how long we can still "
"live here."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:20
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:20
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"With the destruction of the village, all we need now is a Cyclops raiding "
"party to attack us!  Then our fate would be sealed and we would certainly "
"perish!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:21
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:21
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A strange cave has opened north of the village.  It appeared shortly after "
"the sea of fire devastated the village.  Strange creatures have been seen "
"entering and leaving this cave.  I wonder what is inside it?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:22
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:22
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Under Sir Charles Quixote's guidance we will rid this region of the threat "
"of Dragons once and for all!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:23
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:23
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Nagas have become more and more of a problem while we are hunting.  It's not"
" bad enough that we have to stay watchful for Dragons attacking us from the "
"sky, now we have to worry about Nagas ranging out from their vault."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:24
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:24
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Sir Charles Quixote sent us out to train under the guidance of Jeric "
"Whistlebone.  Some day I hope to be as great a knight as he!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:25
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:25
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There have been strange flashes of light from the north for many nights now."
"  Zanthora the Mad Necromancer is most certainly brewing up trouble for "
"someone.  I certainly hope it is not for us of the Guild of Necromancers!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:26
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:26
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There was another vampire attack last night.  I wish we didn’t have to put "
"up with them!  But the Guild of Necromancers has their alliance with the "
"Nosferatu, and we cannot retaliate.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:27
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:27
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There has not been a battle with the Temple of the Sun in years.  I hope "
"they are not planning another assault upon the Guild.  It took years for us "
"to recover from the last battle!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:28
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:28
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Glory to all who bathe in the cleansing light of the Sun! Do you walk in the"
" path of its light?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:29
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:29
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There was a tremendous wind storm that devastated most of the forest to the "
"north of here!  It has driven basilisks, will o' wisps and unicorns closer "
"to the temple!  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:30
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:30
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Be gone!  We have no use for you here, unless we uses you to feed the "
"wyverns!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:31
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:31
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"We have not had any travelers from Balzathar Lair since the canyon filled "
"with water.  I wonder if any of them survived the flood!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:32
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:32
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Better watch out!  The Dread Pirate Stanley doesn't like strangers snooping "
"around our island!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:33
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:33
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If we can conquer Dagger Wound Island, then nothing will stop us from "
"raiding Ravenshore and even the city of Alvar itself!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:34
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:34
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I saw torches last night at the old ruined fort across the bay last night."
"   I wonder what people were doing out there?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:35
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:35
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks for helping us empty the lair!  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:36
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:36
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Now that the water is gone, we can begin putting our lives in order.  But "
"what if the flood comes back?  Are we still safe?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:37
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:37
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Our herd leader, Masul, will certainly wish to speak with you if you haven't"
" already found him.  Seek him out and he may reward you for helping us."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:38
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Group 36"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:39
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Group 37"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:40
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:40
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Nothing to see here… move along."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:41
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:41
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Walk in the Light, friends."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:42
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:42
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Welcome to our holy retreat. If you have business with our order, seek out "
"the head priest, Oskar Tyre. His office is in the temple."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:43
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:43
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"What are you bothering me for? Talk to the Guildmaster, Sandro. He deals "
"with guests. Not me!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:44
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:44
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Out of my way, cretin! You interrupt my thoughts, and I'm thinking about "
"important matters!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:45
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:45
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I hope that this war against the Dragons never ends!  Charles Quixote pays "
"mercenaries like myself very well for our services."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:46 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:47
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:46
#: mm8/Data/10LocLANG.EnglishT/NPCNEWS.txt.py:47
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Our king, Deftclaw, has given you his protection, but watch your step. Cause"
" any trouble, and I will make a snack out of you."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:48
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Group 46"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:49
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Group 47"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:50
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Group 48"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:51
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Group 49"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:54
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:3
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good luck in the contest!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:55
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:4
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I wish Brent knew how to make a red potion."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:56
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:5
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You'd better watch out."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:57
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:6
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Don't cause any trouble."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:58
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:7
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Congratulations!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:59
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:8
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks for trading with us!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:60
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Group 7"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:61
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Group 8"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:62
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Group 9"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:63 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:64
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:12
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:13
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "So you are the new Lords of Harmondale?  How may I serve you?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:65
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:14
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Come to study with us under the Masters?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:66
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:15
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome to the capitol of Steadwick! 'Ware the griffins!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:67
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:16
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You are welcome in Pierpont, the Elven capitol."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:68
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:17
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings!  Head up the stairs to Pierpont and enjoy!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:69
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:18
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Beware the Walking Dead in the region!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:70
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:19
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yer welcome here I think…then again…"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:71
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:20
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Come to learn from the best Wizards in Erathia?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:72
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:21
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings.  Lots of golems around these days!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:73
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:22
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Study with the best and visit all the buildings here!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:74
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:23
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Tranquility and rest await you here in Celeste."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:75
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:24
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome!  Be sure you don’t have a \"falling out\" while you here!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:76
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:25
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome to the Pit!  Who says being dead is bad?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:77
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:26
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Pit is the only place I know of that lets us live in peace!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:78
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:27
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings! Necromancy is evil?  It’s a relative, don’t you think?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:79
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:28
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome to Mulder!  Enjoy your time with us."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:80
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:29
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Have you journeyed far?  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:81
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:30
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello!  Did you come through the tunnels from Stone City?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:82
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:31
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello there?  Checked your purse lately? Let me check it for you…"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:83
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:32
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Some Wacko around here has the boat schedule, I'm sure!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:84
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:33
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "As a citizen of the city of Tidewater, I welcome you."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:85
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:34
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Greetings, heard any word of Regnan Pirates?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:86
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:35
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I heard there was a gate built to the Ancients!  I wonder what they look "
"like."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:87
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:36
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I've heard rumors of goblins and undead armed with ancient weapons "
"threatening to conquer Erathia!  How dreadful!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:88
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:37
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Congratulations on completing the gate!  Erathia is in your debt!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:89
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:38
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Congratulations on completing the forge!  Victory will surely be ours!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:90 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:91 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:92 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:93 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:94 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:95 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:96 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:97 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:98 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:99 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:100 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:101 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:102 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:103
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:39
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:40
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:41
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:42
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:43
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:44
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:45
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:46
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:47
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:48
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:49
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:50
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:51
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCNEWS.TXT.py:52
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:104
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:3
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I've heard that the abandoned keep on the hill is now home to a pack of "
"goblins.  The keep was built to keep the goblins away, so how could this "
"possibly happen?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:105
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:4
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A day's travel west of here is a new Temple dedicated to Baa.  I've heard "
"that bad things happen to rich people that travel near there."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:106
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:5
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The passes through the hills to the west are filled with bandits, travelling"
" on foot through there can be dangerous."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:107
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:6
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Ocean travel around here can be dangerous because of the sea serpents and "
"water elementals that roam the oceans."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:108
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:7
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The High Council in Free Haven should really consult the Oracle to find out "
"why the Ironfists have lost the Mandate of Heaven."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:109
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:8
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Prince Nicolai isn't even in charge anymore– Regent Humphrey makes all of "
"the decisions.  It's not fair to blame Nicolai for all the problems."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:110
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:9
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The two solstices are days of considerable magical importance.  The summer "
"solstice is on June 21st, and the winter solstice is on December 21st."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:111
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:10
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The stables at Castle Ironfist can take you to the Arena, an ancient place "
"where warriors can test their prowess."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:112
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:11
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Goblins are weak creatures, but they tend to attack in large numbers."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:113
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:12
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Though their physical attacks are weak, these mages can cast various "
"elemental attack spells."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:114
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:13
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A powerful artifact, Mordred is a dagger that possesses the ability to steal"
" the health of its victim and transfer that vitality to its wielder."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:115
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:14
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Albert Newton in Mist handles the promotion of Sorcerers to Wizards."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:116
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:15
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The abandoned temple northwest of town used to be occupied by the Temple of "
"Baa, but they moved out in a hurry one day last year.  Now there's nothing "
"but snakes, bats, and huge spiders."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:117
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:16
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"When the Temple of Baa moved out of that old temple outside of town, all of "
"the little problems we've been having just…went away.  I tell you, there's "
"something unwholesome about those people.  I'm glad they're gone."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:118
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:17
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A wizard friend of mine told me the Temple of Baa was laying curses on our "
"town from the abandoned temple just outside town.  One day they tried to lay"
" the Curse of Endless Vermin on us, only they did something wrong and it "
"backfired, infesting their own temple instead.  They moved righty-o quick "
"once that happened."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:119
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:18
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I heard the Temple of Baa abandoned that old temple so quickly they didn't "
"have time to take all their stuff.  It should all still be down there, if "
"you're brave enough to go look for it.  There's a lot of nasty monsters in "
"the way, though, so be careful if you go."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:120
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:19
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It's been quite a while since New Sorpigal was raided by goblins, but with "
"goblins living in the very place meant to protect us from them, it can't be "
"too long before we're attacked again, can it? "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:121
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:20
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"An evil guild of mages has been searching the southeast end of our peninsula"
" for signs of the fabled Fountain of Magic.  They attack anyone who comes "
"near to scare off potential rivals.  Be very careful if you travel in that "
"direction!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:122
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:21
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The three fountains we have here in town are said to draw their water from a"
" spring touched by the gods.  Each one is magical and beneficial to drink "
"from."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:123
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:22
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A raiding party of goblins has staked out the west bridge, hoping to rob and"
" kill travelers.  They aren't very subtle– you can see them from a mile "
"away– but they ARE dangerous.  Watch your step!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:124
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:23
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Our town was founded centuries ago as the last major town in Enroth.  We "
"have historically been a point from which colony ships left for the rest of "
"the world."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:125
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:24
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The fruit on the trees in the orchards of our fair town is quite tasty, and "
"free for all to take.  You should try it sometime!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:126
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:25
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Beware of travelling to the islands just off our north shore.  The waters "
"sometime have dangerous monsters, and the islands are none too hospitable, "
"either.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:127
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:26
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It's been decades since we were last attacked by pirates from the islands of"
" Regna, and I guess it's about time for us to be attacked again, what with "
"the king missing and all."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:128 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:153
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:27
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:52
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Buccaneers' Lair in New Sorpigal and Mist can teach you dagger, merchant, "
"identify, perception, and disarm trap."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:129
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:28
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You can learn dagger, merchant, identify, perception, and disarm trap at "
"protection services in Silver Cove and White Cap."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:130 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:155
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:29
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:54
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Blackshire and Free Haven are homes to the Smugglers' Guild, where you can "
"learn dagger, merchant, identify, perception, and disarm trap."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:131 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:156
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:30
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:55
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Sword, axe, spear, staff, and leather are all taught in Blades' End in both "
"White Cap and New Sorpigal."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:132
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:31
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Duelists' Edge in Mist teaches mace, bow, chain, shield, and body building."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:133
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:32
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Berserker's Fury in Castle Ironfist can teach you bow, shield, chain, plate,"
" and repair item."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:134
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:33
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Fraternal Order of Silver has recently built a keep just south of Mist."
"  They used to be such nice people, but now they're so intent on killing "
"evil they destroy anything that isn't perfect, and that's just about "
"everything."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:135
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:34
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I love living down here!  Lord Newton never remembers to raise taxes."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:136
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:35
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The islands of Bootleg Bay are home to a few cannibal tribes.  People that "
"visit those islands don't return. "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:137
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:36
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Fountain of Magic is supposed to be south of Bootleg Bay, but not many "
"people have ever found it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:138
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:37
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"In the islands south of Mist is the forge of Gharik, one of Archibald's "
"fellow mages.  The place is crawling with elementals– no one ever goes there"
" now."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:139
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:38
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"On an island north of Mist is Castle Alamos, one of the centers of magical "
"study in Enroth.  All sorts of summoning and alchemy occurs in that castle– "
"it's a dangerous place for the casual visitor."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:140
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:39
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A couple of old temples are said to still stand in the jungle islands of "
"Bootleg Bay.  I wonder if anyone still worships in them?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:141
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:40
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Water elementals prowl the waters near Mist.  As if their powerful physical "
"attacks aren't enough, they can also fire Ice Bolts from a distance."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:142
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:41
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"This axe is a hero's dream.  It's enchanted to slay dragons and devils, and "
"does so quite well.  Unfortunately, owners of the axe tend to find such "
"creatures more often then they'd like to."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:143
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:42
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Not many people make it to wizard, and even fewer are promoted to arch "
"mages.  Albert Newton must ask the impossible of those looking to be "
"promoted."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:144
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:43
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Mist was originally intended to be a customs and trading port for dealings "
"with the Eastern islands and countries.  Piracy has severely cut into that "
"trade, so we're not as prosperous as we should be."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:145
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:44
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"About 200 miles to the east of us lie the Regnan Islands.  They are "
"inhabited with pirates ruled by an 'emperor' who 'taxes' passing ships that "
"pass near their territory.  The Regnans produce almost nothing on their own,"
" with the exception of weapons and mercenaries."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:146
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:45
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I hear you can make a potion of supreme protection by mixing an orange "
"potion with a green potion."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:147
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:46
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Melody Silver was recently imprisoned by the Silver Helms in their new "
"outpost south of Mist.  They've been acting awfully strange lately, and it's"
" terrible that they seized such a nice young woman.  Someone's got to do "
"something about those people!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:148
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:47
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Silver Helms, founded by John Silver, were originally organized to fight"
" brigands and murderers, but they've been harassing citizens for even the "
"most petty crimes recently. "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:149
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:48
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Most of the international trade on our island is with the Kingdom of "
"Erathia, homeland of our good Queen Catherine.  Erathia is the source of "
"most of our precious metals and stone."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:150
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:49
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Years of practicing high sorcery can erode the memory of the sorcerer "
"severely, and there is no cure for it.  Even if there was, it's unlikely the"
" victim would remember to use it! "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:151
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:50
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Albert Newton was promoted to his current position because of his strong "
"support for Roland during the Succession War, even though Archibald offered "
"him much sorcerous knowledge.  Lord Newton must surely be a good man to have"
" refused to support the wicked Archibald, even though it looked like "
"Archibald was going to win."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:152
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:51
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Although Lord Newton seems weak and forgetful these days, it's good to "
"remember that he was once one of the greatest sorcerers in the land, perhaps"
" the greatest sorcerer ever!  They say that Lord Newton has forgotten more "
"sorcerous knowledge than Archibald ever knew, excepting the school of dark "
"magic."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:154
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:53
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You can learn dagger, merchant, identify, perception, and disarm trap at "
"Protection Services in Silver Cove and White Cap."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:157
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:56
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Duelists' Edge in Free Haven teaches mace, bow, chain, shield, and repair "
"item."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:158
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:57
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Berserker's Fury in Silver Cove can teach you sword, bow, shield, plate, and"
" body building."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:159
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:58
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you're skilled enough, Calvin Black can teach you ways to improve your "
"staff skill.  He lives in a house right near the Imp Slapper."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:160
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:59
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"When Gonzalo isn't spending time in the Imp Slapper, he teaches spear "
"expertise."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:161
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:60
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you're looking to gain expertise in leather armor, Arthur teaches right "
"near the Buccaneers' Lair."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:162
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:61
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Bernard teaches expert repair skill just south of the Duelists' Edge."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:163
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:62
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The weird creatures that have been summoned around here make people forget "
"that Alamos was the home of some of the best alchemists in the world.  "
"Powerful items must be kept in that castle."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:164
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:63
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"One of the islands to the west has a strange circle of stones.  I think "
"that's used for the Ceremony of the Sun, one of the requirements in Druid "
"promotions."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:165
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:64
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The waters around Castle Alamos teem with sea serpents that attack ships "
"with their icy breath."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:166
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:65
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Percival is the ultimate ranged attack weapon.  With its rapid fire and "
"dangerous explosive attack, it can wipe out large numbers of enemies at a "
"safe distance."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:167
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:66
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"These annoying creatures are immune to magic, but not immune to a good sword"
" blow."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:168
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:67
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The old Dwarf King is in exile now, but I'll bet he wants his throne back "
"pretty badly."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:169
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:68
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Snergle hid the key to the innermost chambers of his caverns in the iron "
"mines to the west."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:170
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:69
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Wilbur Humphrey is so scared that something will happen to Nicolai, the "
"Prince has not been allowed to leave the castle in months."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:171
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:70
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"After Corlagon's defeat in the Succession Wars, he retired to his Estate in "
"the Mire of the Damned to study sorcery.  Rumor has it that he became a lich"
" hoping to survive until Archibald could return."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:172
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:71
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Shadow Guild, an upstart Thieves' Guild, supposedly has a hideout near "
"Castle Ironfist.  I'm sure Anthony Stone would love to see that hideout "
"destroyed."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:173
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:72
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I'm surprised that Nicolai hasn't asked the Oracle for advice; I doubt "
"Regent Humphrey has all the answers."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:174
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:73
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There's still no news on when Catherine will be back from her trip to "
"Erathia."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:175
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:74
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"King Roland's Yacht, the Queen Catherine, hasn't left port in years.  Is it "
"even still seaworthy?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:176
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:75
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Lizardmen prowl around the swampy areas south of Castle Ironfist.  They use "
"bows, but the most powerful are wizards that will cast Lightning Bolts when "
"threatened."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:177
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:76
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Arena of Enroth can be reached through the stables in Ironfist.  You can"
" fight almost any kind of monster there, if you have the taste for that sort"
" of thing.  Lots of people would go every day, but the Arena is only open on"
" Sundays."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:178
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:77
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A useful shield that unerringly blocks missile attacks and makes its user "
"more likely to land blows in battle."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:179
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:78
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Wilbur Humphrey, in Roland's absence, handles the promotions of all paladins"
" to crusaders."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:180
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:79
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Lord Corlagon was Archibald's greatest lieutenant during the Succession War,"
" and after his side lost, he retired to his mansion in the swamps somewhere."
"  It is said that he performed the Ritual of the Endless Night and became a "
"lich a couple of years ago."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:181
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:80
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Wilbur Humphrey is Foremost Paladin of the land.  Though many say he is too "
"naïve and unfit to rule while King Roland is gone, people say he is utterly "
"fearless and honest.  I personally think we couldn't possibly find a better "
"man for the job!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:182
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:81
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The fabulous Circus of the Sun usually sets up a few day's travel down the "
"trade road leading north from Castle Ironfist.  They are always there in "
"December of each year."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:183
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:82
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There are highwaymen plying the trade road brazenly near the castle.  The "
"Regent must be mightily distracted to permit these ruffians to rob innocent "
"travelers right beneath his nose!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:184
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:83
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Seer lives in a hut on a mountain near the source of the Silver River "
"that runs from the Steel Mountains, past Castle Ironfist, and into the "
"ocean.  It is said that he helps those who are lost."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:185
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:84
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Rocklin, former King of the Dwarves, has been deposed by a dwarf named "
"Snergle.  Snergle renamed the mines and caverns formerly operated by Rocklin"
" to, predictably, Snergle's Mine and Snergle's Caverns.  You can find both "
"of those places west of the mountains near Castle Ironfist called the Steel "
"Mountains."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:186
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:85
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The swamps of Enroth are home to all manner of unwholesome monsters, many of"
" them undead.  Carry fire and tread lightly if you should ever have to "
"venture there!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:187
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:86
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The road between Castle Ironfist and New Sorpigal has become quite unsafe.  "
"Ordinarily, we only have one group of bandits preying upon travelers…but "
"these days we have not one, not two, but THREE groups of bandits!  First, "
"there is that hideous Temple of Baa, then we have the Dragoon hideout near "
"the south shore somewhere, and finally we have an unauthorized Thieves' "
"Guild open for business near the Castle!  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:188
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:87
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Newt teaches expert leather skill south of Castle Ironfist."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:189
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:88
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You can learn expert chain skill from Rich just south of Castle Ironfist."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:190
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:89
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A little south of Castle Ironfist are four small houses.  Benito teaches "
"expert plate skill in the northmost one."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:191
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:90
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Edgar will teach sufficiently skilled shield users expert techniques."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:192
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:91
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Aaron teaches expert sword wielding right next to the weapon shop in Castle "
"Ironfist."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:193
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:92
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Expert axe is taught by Stephan in the training grounds."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:194
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:93
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Helen lives with her friend Tracy right between the King's Crown and the "
"Eagle's Eye."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:195
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:94
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Tyler teaches expert disarm right across the street from the training "
"grounds in Castle Ironfist."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:196
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:95
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Leon teaches expert identify right across the street from the training "
"grounds in Castle Ironfist."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:197
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:96
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Olaf lives in a small house behind Castle Ironfist, and teaches expert body "
"building from there."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:198
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:97
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Elton teaches expert learning in one of the towers of Castle Ironfist."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:199
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:98
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Walter teaches expert diplomacy in one of the towers of Castle Ironfist."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:200
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:99
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Behind the King's Crown you can find Terrance Smith.  He'll teach skilled "
"dagger users a few new tricks."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:201
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:100
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I hear there's a reward out for the ones who can put down the Dragoon "
"highwaymen plying the road near the south shore.  Some merchant's offering a"
" LOT of money for the return of his stolen merchandise!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:202
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:101
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A small order of monks has grown just south of Bootleg Bay, called the Order"
" of the Fist."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:203
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:102
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The islands of Bootleg Bay hide a pile of pirate treasure.  That is, if you "
"can get past the cannibals and actually find it…"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:204
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:103
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The location of the Fountain of Magic is still a mystery.  For some reason, "
"the people that find it never reveal its location."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:205
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:104
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Church of the Sun used to have a temple on an island in Bootleg Bay."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:206
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:105
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A powerful crown, Arthur not only boosts all its wearer's physical "
"characteristics, but also their spell points."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:207
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:106
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I've heard that you need to slay an elder dragon to be promoted from "
"Crusader to Hero.  No wonder there are so few Heroes around!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:208
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:107
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The temple of Tsantsa can be found on one of the large islands south of "
"Silver Cove.  The people that live on that island like to sacrifice captives"
" to their beastly god Tsantsa, and then shrink their heads in the pools of "
"disgusting chemicals they keep in their temple.  The islanders are quite "
"hostile, so be sure to kiss your loved ones goodbye if you have plans to "
"visit the island."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:209
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:108
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Long abandoned by the Church of the Sun, their temple still stands on a "
"large island east of Free Haven.  A small order of confused monks, "
"misapprehending the true nature of the temple, have somehow made peace with "
"the islanders and moved into the temple– bringing a stolen holy artifact "
"with them.  Now the old temple's insidious magic has affected their minds, "
"making them believe they must defend the temple to the death.  The monks are"
" very unfriendly these days, and attack all who trespass."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:210
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:109
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Preston teaches expert chain skill just east of the Goblin's Tooth."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:211
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:110
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Shoshi can teach you new perception tricks from his house just east of the "
"Goblin's Tooth."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:212
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:111
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Winston used to be a member of that new clerical order down here, but he "
"quit.  Apparently he left something behind because he's looking for someone "
"to go back to the Temple of the Fist for him.  He's lives in one of the "
"antechambers of the House of Healing now."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:213
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:112
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Cedric Druthers' splinter group of druids perform ceremonies in a cave west "
"of Silver Cove."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:214
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:113
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The stronghold of the Fraternal Order of Silver is located near Silver Cove."
"  The Silver Helms seem more violent lately, I wonder why that is?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:215
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:114
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Warlord's Fortress is to the northwest of Silver Cove.  Only the "
"strongest warriors are enlisted into his army."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:216
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:115
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Shadow Guild supposedly has a large guild right near Castle Stone.  I'm "
"surprised Anthony Stone hasn’t discovered its location yet."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:217
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:116
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Not many ships travel to Castle Alamos.  Most captains are afraid of the "
"strange creatures that prowl around the northern seas."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:218
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:117
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Guilds of Light can be found in Silver Cove and Blackshire and Guilds of "
"Dark can be found in Winter Cap and Blackshire."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:219
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:118
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Diamond Gargoyles are the toughest gargoyles around.  They're impossible to "
"kill with physical attacks, so you should use magic to kill them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:220
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:119
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Druids can cast a variety of elemental spells when angered, and are often "
"slightly shielded from magical attacks."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:221
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:120
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"These legendary boots enable their wearer to move faster and react quicker."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:222
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:121
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"To be promoted to Arch Druid, a Greater Druid needs to perform the Ceremony "
"of the Moon in the Temple of the Moon near Free Haven."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:223
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:122
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The fortress of the Warlord watches over the source of the Calimar river as "
"it winds its way past Silver Cove and empties into Bootleg Bay.  Originally "
"established to protect a town planned for that region, the fortress became a"
" magnet for mercenaries and criminals after the town failed and all the "
"settlers moved south to greener pastures."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:224
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:123
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Monolith overlooks the Silver road that leads from Silver Cove to Free "
"Haven.  It's been an object of fascination and occasional worship for ages."
"  A long time ago, some group of druids carved a home out of the giant rock,"
" and it has been inhabited by various groups since then.  The druids who "
"currently live there were experimenting with some kind of new magic, and I "
"think something may have gone wrong.  They've been avoiding contact with the"
" outside world for some time now, and refuse to allow visitors to enter the "
"Monolith."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:225
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:124
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The town of Silver Cove got its start as a fishing and trading village a few"
" hundred years ago.  With time, our little village grew up to be a full-"
"fledged town.  We have ample room to expand the town, and the land around us"
" is fertile and easy to farm.  We are just a little distant from the rest of"
" the Kingdom, though."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:226
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:125
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Lady of Silver Cove often seems more interested in amassing her fortune "
"than governing well, but I don't think it's so simple.  She often spends a "
"lot of wealth on town improvements and security, so I guess she can't be all"
" bad."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:227
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:126
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Silver Helm vigilantes have occupied a fortress just north of Silver "
"Cove.  Accusing Lady Fleise of the sin of greed, the Silver Helms have begun"
" to attack her caravans travelling between Silver Cove and Free Haven.  I'm "
"sure she's none too happy about it..."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:228
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:127
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Be careful of travelling the waters north and east of Silver Cove– they're "
"inhabited by giant, man-eating sea serpents!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:229
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:128
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Spring Equinox is on March 20th, and the Autumn Equinox is on September "
"23rd.  It's said that these dates are important magical events."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:230
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:129
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The White Rock Islands north of Silver Cove have long been abandoned by "
"civilized humans, and are now home to the monsters and madmen.  Druids "
"occasionally risk their lives and journey to those islands looking for the "
"fabled Circle of Stones so they can perform the Ceremony of the Sun."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:231
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:130
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Silver Helms have been attacking everyone they see as less than 100% "
"behind their fight against evil.  I don't know about you, but I think such "
"an extreme position can't be a good thing– what's Sir John Silver thinking?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:232
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:131
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The druids of the Monolith have made a pact with the Netherworld– I know, "
"because I met a druid who escaped from there one night.  He says unspeakable"
" things are happening inside the Monolith, and if something isn't done soon,"
" the outside world may soon learn more than it ever wanted to know about the"
" secrets of the ancient place."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:233
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:132
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Tina lives with her daughter just east of Town Hall.  She teaches light "
"expertise to skilled apprentices."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:234
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:133
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You can learn expert repair just west of the Mercenary Guild from Cyrus "
"Montebleu."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:235
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:134
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Clyde teaches expert meditation skill right across the street from the Self "
"Guild."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:236
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:135
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Sigriv can teach you expert techniques with the spear just south of the "
"training grounds."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:237
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:136
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I heard that Eleanor wants the evil druids kicked out of the Monolith to the"
" west, and she's willing to offer a reward to the people that do it.  She's "
"on the east side of town if you want to know more."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:238
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:137
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The home of the Necromancers; no one travels to Castle Darkmoor anymore "
"unless they're looking for undead.  I can't imagine the village of Darkmoor "
"surviving much longer without any trade from the rest of Enroth."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:239
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:138
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The mountains to the west keep all the horrible creatures of Dragonsand from"
" rampaging across the rest of Enroth."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:240
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:139
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Snergle isn't a good leader, but none of the dwarves dare to stand up to "
"him."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:241
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:140
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Terrax never left Darkmoor after he became a lich.  He could very well still"
" be inside researching new magical spells."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:242
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:141
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The ghosts that haunt the Mire of the Damned can age you past your years "
"with a single touch."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:243
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:142
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Harpies will curse their unlucky victims.  Fortunately, they're pretty easy "
"to kill."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:244
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:143
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Even though skeletons are the weakest undead monster, some of them can curse"
" you or fill your hearts with unnatural fear."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:245
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:144
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A ring useful for either a cleric or paladin, Igraine boosts the effect of "
"their spells."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:246
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:145
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Osric requires a test of skill for promotion to champion.  Few ever succeed "
"in that test."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:247
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:146
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Connie teaches expert axe skill just outside Darkmoor village."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:248
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:147
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Casey teaches expert merchant skill upstairs in the south of Darkmoor "
"village."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:249
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:148
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Jack teaches expert mace skill across the street from Smoke and Mirrors."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:250
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:149
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Avinril was an important dwarf until the new king Snergle kicked him out.  "
"He's looking for revenge now, and needs help.  I know you can find him in "
"the Haunt out by one of the dwarf mines."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:251
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:150
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Church of the Moon had a temple to the west.  Now, Cedric Druthers' "
"druids use the temple for their ceremonies."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:252
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:151
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The sewers under Free Haven are crawling with thieves and pests.  I can't "
"imagine anyone WANTING to live in a sewer."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:253
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:152
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I've heard that a strange ship sails in the middle of Temper's lake."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:254
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:153
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Cedric Druthers' druids now occupy an old temple of the Church of the Moon "
"to the west of Free Haven."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:255
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:154
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The High Council has not once visited the Oracle since these disasters have "
"started happening.  The wisdom of the Oracle could certainly be used now."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:256
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:155
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The pass to White Cap and Castle Stromgard is now patrolled by renegade "
"ogres and greedy humans."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:257
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:156
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"No surprise, archers will fire arrows at you.  However, some archers prefer "
"to use flaming arrows, and the best of them can actually cast Fireball."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:258
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:157
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A sorcerer or archer's best friend, this amulet boosts the effect of "
"elemental magic."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:259
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:158
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Osric Temper handles all the promotions of knights in Enroth."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:260
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:159
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The High Council meets in Free Haven to represent the Lords of Enroth and "
"handle the important business of the Realm.  With trouble brewing in the "
"west, you would think they'd meet more frequently, but they still limit "
"their hours as though nothing were happening!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:261
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:160
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Of all the Lords of Enroth, Osric Temper is the most concerned with handling"
" the devils that have been attacking the western towns and villages.  I "
"personally believe he is the only Lord with his head screwed on straight "
"these days!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:262
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:161
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I hear there's a Thieves' Guild in the city with a trap door leading into "
"the Free Haven city sewer.  They must use it to distribute all their stolen "
"loot around town."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:263
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:162
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Circus of the Sun usually sets up a few days south of Castle Temper on "
"the west side of the Crescent River.  They stay there during August of every"
" year."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:264
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:163
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Though small, the village of Rockham serves as a trading post and rest stop "
"for people travelling around the Kingdom.  'Though all roads may lead to "
"Free Haven, nearly every traveler has to pass through Rockham to get there."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:265
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:164
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"When Ethric the Necromancer…died, he left instructions for his body to be "
"placed in a tomb he had built next to the mountains south of the Pearblossom"
" river.  It's said that he rose from the dead a few days later in a sort of "
"infernal miracle.  Since then, the tomb has become a spiritual sink where "
"all manner of lost souls drift to after death.  There they languish, "
"mindlessly attacking the living in defense of their new master Ethric the "
"Mad."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:266
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:165
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"An unsavory company of mercenaries has moved into a fortification built by "
"Roland during the Succession War, near Crescent Lake.  Far as I know, the "
"mercenaries haven't done anything wrong yet, but their presence is ominous, "
"don't you think?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:267
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:166
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Free Haven is the oldest and most prosperous city in the Kingdom.  With a "
"natural harbor and the Oracle, it was only common sense for people to gather"
" here since the Silence."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:268
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:167
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Glimmervale Lake has been the source of many supernatural sightings lately."
"  People say the sightings are caused by the tampering of the Necromancer's "
"Guild, disbanded now for ten years.  Who knows what damage they caused "
"before King Roland put a stop to their evil?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:269
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:168
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Temple Stone in Free Haven was recently burnt to the ground by a group of "
"monks trying to steal the sacred chalice from the temple.  They fled east by"
" boat, and nobody's seen them since."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:270
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:169
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I don't know if you've noticed, but those creepy followers of Baa keep "
"popping in and out of buildings around town in the strangest manner.  Could "
"be that they've located one of their temples in the city sewer system."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:271
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:170
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Maybe there really is something to the notion that evil is down, while good "
"is up.  Both the followers of Baa and members of the Shadow Guild can be "
"found in the city sewers.  Would that we have a big flood one day to wash "
"all that trash out to sea!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:272
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:171
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Beware bandits on the road to Blackshire!  Ever since the King went off to "
"who knows where, criminals have been plying the roads between all the major "
"cities."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:273
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:172
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Liches are the only form of the living dead that actually chooses to be "
"living dead.  A lich is the rotting skeleton of a powerful cleric or "
"sorcerer, held together by necromantic rites performed during life.  A "
"relatively new monster, it is said that Ethric the Mad was the first "
"sorcerer to discover and perform the Ritual of the Endless Night, "
"simultaneously becoming the world's first lich and necromancer. <Shuddering>"
" Creepy, huh?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:274
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:173
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The mercenaries living in that stronghold near Castle Temper seem to have a "
"lot of money, because they keep ordering up weapons and supplies.  Someone "
"must be paying them for some reason, but who?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:275
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:174
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I hear the former King of the Dwarves is hiding out in some local tavern, "
"drowning his sorrows after being deposed by Snergle.  A sorry fate for "
"Roland's most steadfast ally during the War!  I'll bet if King Roland were "
"around he would help him out."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:276
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:175
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Timothy teaches expert body magic southwest of the four elemental guilds."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:277
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:176
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Michael teaches expert sword skill just northeast of the body guild."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:278
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:177
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Sylvester can show you new diplomacy tricks south of Town Square."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:279
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:178
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Livia will teach promising merchants a few expert techniques south of Town "
"Square."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:280
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:179
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Takao teaches expert shield just west of the Sharpening Stone."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:281
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:180
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Mynasia teaches expert mind magic southwest of the four elemental guilds."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:282
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:181
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Michele teaches expert spirit magic southwest of the four elemental guilds."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:283
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:182
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You can find expert disarm training from Ivan right near the Smugglers' "
"Guild."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:284
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:183
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Logan lives just northeast of the body guild, and he teaches expert dagger "
"skill."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:285
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:184
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Jack teaches expert fire magic just south of Temple Stone."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:286
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:185
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Woodrow lives just southwest of the mind guild, and he teaches expert plate "
"skill."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:287
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:186
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hitomi teaches expert water magic just south of Temple Stone."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:288
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:187
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Li teaches expert earth magic just south of Temple Stone."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:289
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:188
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Zodahn teaches expert air magic just south of Temple Stone."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:290
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:189
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Zoltan was complaining recently that a new artifact for his collection was "
"stolen by the Dragoons to the south of here.  He's put up a bounty for its "
"return, go to his house just south of Town Square for more information."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:291
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:190
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Gabriel said he was working on a way to reverse some weird undead ritual.  I"
" don't know much about rituals, but I do know that Gabriel lives just south "
"of Temple Stone if you want to ask him about it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:292
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:191
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Carlo's good friend Sherell is lost in Bootleg Bay; he's looking for people "
"to help him out near the docks."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:293
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:192
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Rumor has it that the main Shadow Guild guildhall is located very close to "
"Castle Stone.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:294
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:193
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The pass to the Frozen Highlands is unsafe to travel now because of the "
"ogres and humans that took over Icewind Keep."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:295
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:194
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Magyars are straightforward fighters, but the magyar matrons can attack with"
" a deadly electrical blast."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:296
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:195
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"This seemingly simple mace bursts into flames when used, simultaneously "
"dealing a vicious flame attack on its victim and also protecting its wielder"
" from fire."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:297
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:196
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Anthony Stone, among other things, promotes deserving Clerics to Priests."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:298
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:197
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Erik Von Stromgard is the finest archer in the lands, and as such is given "
"the task of training and promoting archers."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:299
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:198
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Lord Stromgard is without a doubt the greatest archer in the land.  He "
"always competes in the major competitions, and I've never seen him lose.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:300
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:199
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Lord Stone has the dual role of being the High Priest of the Realm and the "
"overseer of underworld activity.  A very strange combination, I suppose, but"
" he certainly does seem to keep the peace.  Long may he live!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:301
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:200
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Icewind Keep was once Lord Stromgard's first castle, but he lost it to an "
"attack of ogres and evil humans about a year ago.  He's moved to his second "
"castle east of White Cap, but they say he's rather bitter about the loss and"
" thinks only of revenge these days."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:302
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:201
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Shadow Guild is a new Thieves' Guild created to challenge Lord Stone's "
"authority over the underworld.  They have two hideouts– one near Castle "
"Ironfist and the other within spitting distance of Castle Stone.  It looks "
"to me like they're spoiling for a fight!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:303
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:202
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"White Cap is the third largest town in Enroth, and it's been suffering ever "
"since Lord Stromgard lost Icewind Keep to the ogres last year.  The ogres "
"keep raiding caravans trying to go through the pass.  If the caravans ever "
"stop, it'll be the end for the town."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:304
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:203
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Sure has been a long time since last summer, I think.  MUCH too long.  "
"Something is wrong with the weather, and I'm beginning to think the gods are"
" punishing us for supporting the Ironfist dynasty!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:305
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:204
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If tales told be true, the Shadow Guild and the Temple of Baa are in cahoots"
" to ruin the Kingdom.  I hear the Temple has been magically extending winter"
" in these parts, and the ritual materials they need are being supplied by "
"the Shadow Guild."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:306
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:205
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you've ever seen a sorcerer try to fly near a town, you may have been "
"treated to the sight of the Dragon Towers shooting him down.  Dragon Towers "
"shoot at anything that flies near a town, because they have trouble telling "
"the difference between a man and a dragon.  Be careful!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:307
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:206
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It sure is a bad thing that those ogres have control over Icewind keep!  "
"Some of their human allies are archers, and they like to shoot at people "
"going through the pass.  They've been real bad for business at White Cap, "
"believe me."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:308
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:207
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There are a few important passes in the kingdom, and more and more they're "
"controlled by monsters rather than the king's men.  If things go the way "
"they're going much longer, we'll have to pay taxes to the devils instead of "
"the king!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:309
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:208
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A master of air I spoke with some time ago claims that someone is tinkering "
"with the weather using ritual magic.  He says he traced the magic back to "
"one of those temples of Baa that've been springing up all over the place "
"recently.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:310
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:209
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The mountains around here have some mighty strange hermits living in them "
"here and there.  Most are crazy, but a few go there to meditate on truths "
"not meant for mortal man to know."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:311
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:210
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you look carefully in the mountains of this Kingdom, you might come "
"across a pass that can cut days off your travel."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:312
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:211
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Both Lord Stromgard and Lord Stone were key supporters of King Roland during"
" the Succession Wars.  They owe their current positions to that support, and"
" I think they have been amongst the most conscientious of the Lords of the "
"Realm."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:313
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:212
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Dickson teaches expert mace just west of Castle Stromgard."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:314
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:213
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Jed teaches expert bow just west of Castle Stromgard."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:315
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:214
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Morton teaches expert dark magic in the southwest of White Cap."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:316
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:215
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I've heard that Abdul has his resort in the south of Dragonsand.  Some "
"resort!  It's probably filled with dragons."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:317
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:216
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There's a strange pyramid in the middle of Dragonsand.  No one has any idea "
"who built it, though."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:318
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:217
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Wyrms move very quickly on the ground, but cannot fly.  They attack with a "
"poisonous breath attack."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:319
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:218
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Fire Lizards are just one of a variety of draconian creatures found in "
"Dragonsand."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:320
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:219
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Wielders of Cronos gain an incredible boost to their vitality.  They'll need"
" anything they can get, because troubles and misfortune constantly follow "
"this axe."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:321
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:220
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A cave near Blackshire opened about the same time that people in the town "
"started disappearing."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:322
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:221
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The people of Blackshire have fallen under a terrible curse– they turn into "
"werewolves at night!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:323
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:222
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"An old temple sits in the center of Star Island.  Strangely enough, the "
"number of statues on the island has slowly increased over time."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:324
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:223
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Werewolves are simply people that turn into a half-man, half-beast creature "
"at night.  They are especially powerful under a full moon."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:325
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:224
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Air elementals flitter about in the valley between the Frozen Highlands and "
"Dragonsand.  Though the weakest elementals, they're fast and have a nasty "
"electrical attack."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:326
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:225
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The sword of a mighty warrior, Hercules confers a huge boost to might and "
"endurance, but at the cost of the wielder's intellect."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:327
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:226
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"No one has been promoted to high priest in ages.  I wonder what Anthony "
"Stone requires from Priests for that promotion?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:328
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:227
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The island at the center of Star Lake is home to some monsters straight from"
" the heart of hell!  I heard about someone who rowed out there one night "
"with some friends and these huge snake creatures came boiling up out of the "
"ground.  They had to but look you in the eye to turn you right to stone!  "
"Anyway, this guy was the only one to make it back alive, he says, and he did"
" it by running and not looking back! "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:329
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:228
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A terrible curse has befallen the people in this area, and everyone thinks "
"they know the source– it's that new cave that opened itself up in the side "
"of the mountain south of town.  Someone needs to go in there and end the "
"curse, but bravery's at a premium in Blackshire, these days."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:330
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:229
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Dragonsand is the home and breeding ground of the dragons of Enroth.  Never "
"will you find a more fierce or terrible monster than a dragon, and never "
"will you find one that is gentle or kind.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:331
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:230
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Circus of the Sun likes to set up alongside the road between Blackshire "
"and Star Lake.  They're around here every year during April.  It's a good "
"show– well worth the money to go see it!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:332
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:231
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The road leading west from Blackshire has gone from the safest road in the "
"Kingdom to the most dangerous.  West of here lies Pleasant Valley, and the "
"name has long since become a joke.  Now that valley is a barren and ruined "
"land, crawling with those hideous new monsters– the devils."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:333
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:232
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Just go west down the road from Blackshire a few days and you're sure to see"
" some devils.  You better be able to run pretty fast, though!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:334
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:233
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Lord Kilburn disappeared while patrolling the road leading from Blackshire "
"to Pleasant Valley.  At least, that's what people are saying.  If you're "
"looking for him, you might want to start looking around there."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:335
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:234
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"We all saw the king fleeing from the devils toward Castle Kriegspire a while"
" back.  Haven't heard from him since.  Sad.  I think the devils will take us"
" all, before long."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:336
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:235
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ambrose teaches expert dark magic in the town of Blackshire."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:337
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:236
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Castle Kriegspire, at one time, was the center of magical experimentation in"
" creating creatures.  Now, it's abandoned and the creatures run rampant "
"inside.  The volcano it rests in was created to keep all the monsters in."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:338
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:237
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Agar, one of Archibald's sorcerers, was the most skilled of the "
"experimenters in Kriegspire.  His monsters are the ones crawling around the "
"castle now.  He left with the rest of the mages, but no one knows where he "
"went to."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:339
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:238
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Though weaker than dragons, drakes are nothing to sneer at.  These flying "
"reptiles have powerful elemental attacks."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:340
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:239
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Some of the minotaurs escaped from Kriegspire and now roam in and around the"
" volcano surrounding the old castle."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:341
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:240
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Earth elementals prowl around the area of Kriegspire.  Free from the mages "
"that summoned them, theses elementals look to destroy whatever they come "
"across."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:342
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:241
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"No armor in the world can match Apollo for protection against elemental "
"spells.  Unfortunately, the armor gains its power from sapping the endurance"
" of its wearer."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:343
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:242
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Superior Temple of Baa was constructed about a year ago against the "
"mountains east of Castle Kriegspire.  Unlike most of their temples, it's "
"closed to the public.  You'll have to join them if you ever want to be let "
"in."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:344
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:243
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The village of Edenbrook wouldn't be around these days if it weren't for "
"King Roland and his men.  They saved it from a horde of devils a little "
"while back."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:345
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:244
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"When the king fled to Castle Kriegspire he was followed by an enormous army "
"of devils.  A couple of days later a few dozen devils were seen leaving the "
"old volcano the castle occupies, but the King himself hasn't been seen "
"since."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:346
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:245
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Rarely do humans and dragons get along, but the death knights have formed "
"some sort of pact with a group of dragons in a keep on the north side of the"
" mountains near Kriegspire."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:347
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:246
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Nicholas can show you expert techniques with the magic of light in the "
"village of Kriegspire."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:348
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:247
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Titans are second in power only to the mighty dragons.  Not only do titans "
"possess an incredible electric attack, they are skilled in mind magic and "
"favor the Psychic Shock spell."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:349
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:248
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Fire elementals seem to like Hermit's Isle, though who would summon them "
"there is a mystery."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:350
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:249
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Although this crown reduces the reaction time of its wearer, it also makes "
"the wearer incredibly resistant to elemental magic."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:351
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:250
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Hermit's Island has recently become home to the Supreme Temple of Baa.  They"
" have found an ancient installation to put their temple in, and are no doubt"
" performing dark experiments as we speak."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:352
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:251
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Dragonsand, the great desert of Enroth, is home to all the worst monsters in"
" the world.  Dragons, titans, and other oversized killer monsters roam the "
"sands freely on whatever errands such creatures find important.  Humans "
"foolish enough to travel the desert learn to run and hide very quickly, or "
"they don't last long."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:353
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:252
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Once the greenest and most fertile of lands in Enroth, Pleasant Valley has "
"fallen under a curse that has caused the plants to wither, the animals to "
"sicken, and the people to leave.  It is a barren land now, and no one wants "
"to live there."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:354
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:253
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Shortly after the Night of Shooting Stars, the blight began to eat away at "
"Pleasant Valley.  In a few short years, nearly all the plants and animals "
"had sickened and died, and the villagers and farmers living in the valley "
"had to move east to find food.  The blight has shown no signs of abating– "
"rather, it has accelerated, and will one day cover the entire continent "
"unless something is done to stop it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:355
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:254
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Most of the devils you see in Pleasant Valley are in fact worker or soldier "
"devils.  They are organized like ants, only they have intelligent leaders.  "
"The leaders can fly, and their best leaders can use human speech and "
"writing."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:356
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:255
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Though powerful, the devils are far from invincible.  King Roland fought and"
" won a battle at Sweet Water Pass by outmaneuvering them and outthinking "
"them.  They're tough, but they die like anything else does when you put a "
"sword through it!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:357
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:256
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"These legendary boots make the wearer a blur, able to react instantly to any"
" situation."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:358
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:257
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The devils seem to swarm around a strange building near the remains of Sweet"
" Water."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:359
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:258
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Although the ruins of the buildings are still there, the town is completely "
"destroyed.  No one lives there anymore."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:360
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:259
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The forest of Blackwoode has been wiped out completely since the night of "
"Shooting Stars."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:361
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:260
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The devils seem to prefer fire attacks and enjoy attacking in large groups."
"  Some of the most powerful can cast spells from the fire school."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:362
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:261
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"This odd amulet will grant its wearer extra vitality, spell points, and "
"luck."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:363
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:262
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Sweet Water used to be the most beautiful town in the kingdom, but no news "
"has come from it since the Night of Shooting Stars.  I think the shooting "
"star landed right on top of the town, leaving no survivors to tell the tale."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:364
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:263
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Oracle had warned of the coming of devils from the sky in writings long "
"ago.  I don't think anyone remembers, and of those who do, no one thinks the"
" Night of Shooting Stars and the devils are connected.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:365
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:264
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I met a man who went to discover the fate of the town of Sweet Water, and he"
" says that the place was burnt to the ground by the devils.  The devils have"
" built a strange tower near the old town, and eerie noises come from it "
"every twenty minutes.  He would have explored further, but there were so "
"many devils near the tower he didn't dare."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:366
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:265
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Have you noticed how Temples of Baa have been sprouting up throughout the "
"kingdom?  They're everywhere, and I for one think it's an ominous "
"development.  Although they offer free healing, they don't seem to be doing "
"it out of kindness– there must be a method to their madness!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:367
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:266
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The queen left quite a while ago for her home country of Erathia.  People "
"are getting worried– what if something happened to her during her trip?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:368
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:267
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Most of the shipping in Enroth follows a set schedule.  If you're in the "
"right place at the right time, the shipping companies can take you great "
"distances quickly and cheaply."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:369
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:268
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The legends say that the great ship used in the Crossing lies buried under a"
" giant stone tomb in the middle of Dragonsand.  There must have been a lake "
"or ocean long ago where the desert is now, for the ship to end up in the "
"middle of the desert!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:370
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:269
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you touch one of the obelisks scattered around the kingdom, you'll get a "
"part of a riddle no one's yet unraveled.  People say that a great treasure "
"lies buried somewhere in Enroth, and the one who finds the answer to the "
"riddle will find the treasure."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:371
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:270
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Beware the Dragon Towers you'll find near every major settlement.  They will"
" shoot a fireball at anyone flying.  I guess they're meant to protect the "
"towns from dragons and other flying monsters, but they can't tell the "
"difference between a man and a monster."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:372
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:271
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Some people are saying the Temple of Baa and the devils are in league!  It "
"makes sense– the temple first appeared a few months after the Night of "
"Shooting Stars, and we all know the devils and that night are related!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:373
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:272
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There's a rumor going 'round that Slicker Silvertongue, Wilbur Humphrey's "
"representative on the High Council, is a traitor.  People are saying he's "
"been seen in several Temples of Baa, and everyone knows the temple is "
"against the king!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:374
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:273
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Weather sure has turned sour since the Night of Shooting Stars.  Every "
"summer seems colder than the last.  Why, I'd venture to say last summer was "
"the coldest winter I've ever experienced!  'Course, that's an exaggeration, "
"but you know what I mean.  Something's wrong!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:375
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:274
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Doesn't it seem there's been more floods and earthquakes since the king "
"disappeared?  It's as though the gods are angry with the king and his "
"dynasty.  Perhaps they have lost the Mandate of Heaven."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:376
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:275
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Though the Temple of Baa may offer free healing, it seems to me that more "
"things go wrong, and more people get hurt, when one of their temples is "
"nearby.  Could it be they are cursing the people near them, and then healing"
" them for some bizarre reason?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:377
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:276
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Have you ever seen Archibald's statue in the library behind Castle Ironfist?"
"  It is amazingly lifelike… almost as though he was turned to stone rather "
"than sculpted."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:378
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:277
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The western province of Pleasant Valley has undergone a shocking "
"transformation in the last few years.  Once it was a rich, fertile farming "
"region.  Now all the plants have died from a terrible blight, and the water "
"has dried up.  All the animals sickened or died, and all the people had to "
"move away to find food to eat."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:379
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:278
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Ancient legends say that all the greatest artifacts from before the Silence "
"came with the ship our distant ancestors used to get here from their "
"homeland.  They say the voyage was so long that three generations of people "
"were born, lived, and died while aboard the ship!  How's that for a whopper "
"of a tale?!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:380
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:279
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Erathia is the second major continent to be settled in the world.  It is a "
"lot wilder and more unsafe than Enroth, and all the little kingdoms there "
"are always bickering and fighting."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:381
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:280
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The islands east of Enroth are all part of the 'Kingdom' of Regna.  They "
"were settled by the most nasty and violent of people hundreds of years ago, "
"and they haven't changed their ways.  They are pirates and mercenaries to a "
"man, and have no regard for the sorrow they cause by siding with petty "
"tyrants and usurpers like Archibald was."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:382
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/NPCNews.txt.py:281
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If the old tales are true, the dwarves were once just like the rest of us, "
"but before the Crossing, the dwarves lived in a place where they and "
"everything around them weighed a lot more.  The stories say this made them "
"very short and very strong, and they haven't changed since."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:383
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:3
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I don't like Mondays."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:384
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:4
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The best armor shop in all of Enroth is the Enchanted Hauberk.  The "
"proprietor's name is Teddy, but he hates to be called that.  Safer to refer "
"to him as Theodore."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:385
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:5
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The best magic shop in the kingdom is Mighty Magicks.  It is possible to "
"find there the most unusual and powerful enchanted items for sale anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:386
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:6
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Be careful with even ordinary objects.  If something is magical, get an "
"expert like me to identify it before you sell it for pennies on the gold "
"piece of its true worth.  You can be surprised by what there is to find out "
"there, and you might sell off something very useful."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:387
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:7
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The lands to the far west of the continent used to be green and fertile, but"
" have wasted to an unhappy land of cracked earth, bad smells, and barren "
"landscapes."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:388
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:8
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Most civilized areas you'll find are in the east.  While there are some "
"small towns and villages located to the west, don't count on finding many."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:389
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:9
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"This ghastly place is named for all of the undead that prowl it.  Rumor has "
"it that people killed in the mire return as undead guardians of the place.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:390
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:10
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There are some places you can't get to by boat, during different times of "
"the year.  You should plan your trips carefully to avoid inconvenience."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:391
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:11
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Many areas of the oceans are home to giant sea serpents.  Though not much "
"danger to ships, they can be lethal to people, water walking or even "
"bystanders on the coast."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:392
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:12
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you are wounded enough, you will fall unconscious.  Taking a wound while "
"unconscious almost always leads to death."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:393
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:13
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Mixing poppysnaps, phirna root, or widoweeps berries with water in an empty "
"potion bottle will make a simple potion.  These simple potions have limited "
"beneficial effects, but are stronger than the herbs by themselves."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:394
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:14
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Let me tell you the effects of the simple potions.  Red potions are minor "
"healing, blue potions are minor spell point gain, and yellow potions are a "
"boost to all seven statistics."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:395
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:15
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Because skills get so difficult to learn once you've achieved a high level "
"in them, it is much more efficient to learn many skills to a moderate level,"
" rather than a couple of skills to a high level."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:396
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:16
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Kriegspire, one of the centers of magical experimentation, has been "
"swallowed by an enormous volcano.  Surely one of their experiments must have"
" gone completely awry."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:397
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:17
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The three most important things to remember in a battle are:  Don't get "
"surrounded, concentrate on killing a single enemy before moving on to "
"another, and don't be afraid to run.  No shame in living another day!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:398
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:18
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A finely crafted weapon is a rare find, but a magic weapon is a treasure "
"indeed.  Magic weapons are often more damaging, faster, and sometimes even "
"have spells imbedded into them.  Your skill is important, but having a great"
" weapon certainly doesn't hurt either."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:399
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:19
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"When fighting in a place that is very hot or cold, try using the opposite "
"kind of spell on your enemies.  Often they are resistant or immune to the "
"element they're used to living in."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:400
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:20
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Some sorcerers have cheated death itself in their attempts to gain power.  "
"These sorcerers trade their lives for eternal life as an undead.   I can't "
"imagine the lust for power that would cause someone to trade their soul.  "
"Liches are powerful and determined; you should be careful fighting them. "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:401
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:21
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Light magic makes up one half of the Mirrored Path.  Light cannot exist "
"without dark, nor dark without light.  The spells in the school of light are"
" what most people would call 'holy.'  It is difficult to find training in "
"this path, but the rewards are certainly worth the effort."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:402
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:22
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Merchants respond to a customer's skill in bargaining.  It's important to "
"only use your best negotiator when you buy or sell anything with a  "
"merchant. "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:403
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:23
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A group of bandits called the Dragoons are now preying on merchants "
"travelling between Free Haven and New Sorpigal."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:404
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:24
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A while back I was exploring the Star Lake area, and saw a bunch of statues "
"on the island at the center of the lake.  They were marvelously carved– the "
"most lifelike statues I've ever seen.  I wonder who put them there?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:405
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:25
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The law of the land is simple:  Do not murder, do not threaten, do not "
"bribe.  Begging is frowned upon, as is keeping company with known criminals."
"  Reputation is everything."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:406
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:26
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Enroth is ruled by a king, and the council of five lords.  These six people "
"handle the laws, rules, and matters of state for all of Enroth."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:407
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:27
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"When someone has a chest or other lock they don't want you to get into, "
"they'll usually trap it rather than lock it.  Everyone knows that a "
"determined thief will eventually get through a lock, but not every "
"determined thief will survive the trap once he opens the chest."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:408
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:28
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Some locks are bound by magical enchantments.  You won't be able to open "
"them, no matter how fine a locksmith you are, unless you have the magical "
"key necessary."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:409 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:434
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:29
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:54
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Have you heard of the Temple of Baa?  They're wonderful!  My family was "
"hungry and they fed us when no one else would.  All we had to do was promise"
" to come back!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:410
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:30
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"People often remark at how lucky I am.  It's not so much that I'm lucky, "
"it's that I look on the bright side of everything.  You'd be amazed at how "
"trivial some of your worst problems are if you look at them from the right "
"angle."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:411
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:31
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Every now and then there's someone who needs to go to a strange place, like "
"Castle Kriegspire.  Like this one fellow the other day, he paid me well to "
"help him and his servants carry stuff over the lip of Kriegspire Mountain "
"and into its center.  His servants didn't look too healthy, either, but they"
" never got tired.  Smelled bad, too."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:412
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:32
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Paradise Valley is no more.  All that's left from the Night of the Shooting "
"Stars is a barren wasteland.  I've seen it, but I didn't have the courage to"
" venture into it.  I'm not sure what sort of acts the people of Paradise "
"Valley did to justify that sort of Heavenly retribution, but they must have "
"been foul indeed."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:413
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:33
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Ah!  There's nothing like sitting next to the fire at home with a glass of "
"wine, my dog at my feet, and a good balance sheet to work on.  That's the "
"life!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:414
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:34
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There's no two ways about it– you always need gold.  Everything has a price;"
" hopefully you can pay it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:415
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:35
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Terrible things have been happening lately.  I heard about a village that "
"was washed away in the recent heavy rains when their local creek overflowed "
"its banks, and the news from Sweet Water is so bad there's been no news– "
"people are saying the entire town was wiped out!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:416
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:36
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I've heard the tales of the supper served to Roland's expedition the night "
"before they left.  I wonder if any of them expected to return based on the "
"accounts I've heard of that feast.  The luxury afforded to those men "
"certainly sounded to me like some sort of last meal."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:417
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:37
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Our horses around here are thankfully very tame, but there are some "
"centaurs– half man, half horse– roaming the countryside of Erathia.  The "
"centaurs like to gather in tribes and make war on the humans and elves "
"living near them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:418
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:38
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The sewers under Free Haven house all sorts of interesting things.  I've "
"heard stories of hideouts, temples, treasure, and well, sewage.  I don’t "
"know which to believe, but it certainly seems like an interesting place."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:419
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:39
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Beware taking long trips for a few days– three planets are in retrograde, "
"and one is actually on its third epicycle stage this month, all while Leo is"
" ascending against Pisces' lateral movement.  Don't say I didn’t warn you!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:420
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:40
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There are some places you can't get to during different parts of the year by"
" boat.  You should plan your trips carefully to avoid inconvenience."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:421
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:41
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Magical flying is constrained to a certain altitude, so certain high "
"mountains will block magical flight.  Given all the advantages of flight, "
"that's really a very minor drawback."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:422
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:42
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The water in the lakes and seas around Enroth is very cold, and even the "
"best swimmers can drown in it.  If you fall in the water, get out as fast as"
" you can!  You can't survive long there, no matter how tough you think you "
"are."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:423
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:43
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"An excellent spell, but unfortunately most towns are in the east, so you "
"won't get very far exploring with this spell.  Of course, if you need to run"
" back to town, this is the easiest way to go."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:424
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:44
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Although they were a heretical religion, their heart was in the right place."
"  The Church helped the poor, healed the sick, and comforted the distraught."
"  But they grew rich, powerful, and prideful, and pride indeed goeth before "
"a fall.  When they attacked their rival, the Church of the Moon, they "
"brought both their enemy and themselves down."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:425
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:45
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It's hard to make a living these days playing music in the taverns.  I've "
"been travelling between the towns for years, but people are really scared "
"these days.  Everyone is afraid to spend money."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:426
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:46
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Boats don't always travel on the schedules or to the destinations you want."
"  If you want personal control over your water travel, the water walk spell "
"is the way to go."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:427
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:47
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The cutlass is a better weapon than the broadsword for many reasons, but the"
" best is the way it's swept backward to deceive your opponent about the "
"length of your weapon's reach.  The smithies of Regna turn out the best "
"cutlasses in the world, you can bet on that, matey!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:428
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:48
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Chadwick, a veteran of the Succession Wars, lives in Free Haven.  He's the "
"most decorated living cavalier in Enroth, and one of Osric's favorite "
"knights."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:429
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:49
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Most games of chance are made to separate fools from their money.  Unless "
"you're a psychic or phenomenally lucky, don't waste your hard earned gold on"
" them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:430
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:50
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"With the death of Roland and rumors of a collapse of the Ironfist Rule, the "
"roads are almost unsafe to travel anymore.  Brigands and bandits of all "
"sorts now prey on anyone travelling too far from the protection of the "
"castles."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:431
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:51
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you must resort to 'special' measures to get someone to talk to you, "
"remember that begging is almost free of consequences.  Some types, however, "
"just won't listen to a beggar, forcing you to try another tack.  Thieves and"
" merchants never tolerate begging."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:432
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:52
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Nicolai Ironfist is my twin brother.  I'll bet you didn't know that, did "
"you?  We were separated a long time ago by our father, Roland.  They've used"
" magic to keep Nicolai looking so young, but he's really my age."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:433
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:53
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Most people like to talk about the sewers of Free Haven as a home for all "
"sorts of thieves.  I doubt it though.  I'd certainly live in a nice house "
"with plenty of butlers and maids if I had my druthers.  Why would I choose "
"to live in a sewer?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:435
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:55
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"We need a real king, not a child.  How can Nicolai be a good ruler when he's"
" still a child?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:436
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:56
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There's not much difference in cloak styles, except a general color or "
"fabric choice.  There is one that stands out,  however, as quite unusual.  "
"That's the Doomsday Cloak, fabricated 80 years ago by the Church of the "
"Moon.  You can recognize it buy it's black interior lining and silver hem.  "
"These cloaks are invariably highly enchanted."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:437
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:57
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Someone has to do all the grunt labor around here.  Too bad that someone is "
"me."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:438
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:58
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"All this cold weather's really got me worried.  It's really unusual, and I'm"
" concerned for the health of my crop."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:439
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:59
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If I had a Heavenly Forge, I could make hundreds of barrels a day and not "
"break a sweat.  I guess those forges were one good thing about the Time of "
"Wonders."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:440
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:60
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"To make strong, excellent pottery, you really need a hot fire.  If it "
"weren't so dangerous, I'd make a trip to Castle Kriegspire to try out the "
"fires they're supposed to have under the castle.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:441
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:61
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"When the storms hit in July, I was completely unprepared for the demand for "
"winter clothes.  Now that I'm ready for the winter demand, it hasn't been "
"all that cold.  I must have done something to anger the Heavens!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:442
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:62
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There are a few different kinds of magical boots that alchemists have been "
"making.  Most of the metallic ones have some sort of enchantment on them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:443
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:63
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Why isn't anyone doing anything about all the bad things happening?  Isn't "
"that what the council is there for?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:444
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:64
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There must be something wrong with this year's grain crops.  I can't seem to"
" find enough sellers of raw wheat and corn to make my business run properly."
"  I don't know how much longer this can go on before I'm broke."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:445
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:65
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The metal weapons aren't the only things to be enchanted.  Wooden weapons, "
"like bows, sometimes have powerful spells placed in them as well."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:446
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:66
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Marble is the finest building material money can buy.  Most of it comes from"
" the hills near Blackshire...   which is too bad, since people are saying "
"there's some sort of terrible curse on the people of that area. Not much "
"work is getting done around there these days."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:447
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:67
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"How can you recognize a goblin pirate? He is the one with the patch over "
"both eyes!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:448
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:68
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Monsters been eating the good game animals, lately.  Lots more monsters than"
" usual."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:449
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:69
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I can't believe how few people will actually part with a little money for a "
"wretch like me.  Is everyone so selfish?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:450
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:70
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Don't tell no one, but I have a cleric friend who heals the brand marks "
"right off the cattle we, ah, borrow from all the ranchers.  Works like a "
"charm!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:451
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:71
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The destruction of Paradise Valley wiped out the grandest forest in Enroth, "
"Blackwoode Forest.  A peaceful place, Blackwoode Forest was full of game.  I"
" made a good living there among the trees.  Now I'm not sure where to hunt."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:452
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:72
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You can't even begin to understand how unpleasant working for the nobility "
"is.  They may have money, but no other client is so pushy, demanding, or "
"uncaring about the way they use your time."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:453
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:73
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Island Empire of Regna hasn't converted to Baa yet.  I'm hoping to "
"travel there to spread the word of Baa."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:454
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:74
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We get all of our important shipments in on Tuesdays."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:455
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:75
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Fortunately, most violent people take their aggressions out in the Arena, "
"and not in the towns."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:456
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:78
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The High Council hasn't consulted the Oracle for years.  The last person to "
"try was Archibald, and the Oracle didn't help him out at all."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:457
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:77
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There is nothing worse than new religions promising the world to the "
"underprivileged.  They are upsetting the applecart and fomenting rebellion."
"  This Temple of Baa that everyone is talking about– now, they're no good.  "
"I do wish the regent would mobilize against them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:458
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:76
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Baa, friend…oh.  Uh, I thought you were a member of my temple.  Sorry, my "
"mistake.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:459
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:79
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I hate school.  My father says I need to work hard so that I can get a good "
"job, maybe even learn to study magic.  Who cares about that?  I just want to"
" play!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:460 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:461
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:3
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:4
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Not to ruin my business, but to be honest, if you think about it, it really "
"pays to only hire us smiths when you need us, rather than carrying us around"
" wherever you go."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:462
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:5
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you ever find an item containing the Lloyd's Beacon spell, remember that "
"the locations you are able to transport to are based per person.  That means"
" that even a non-spell using person could have a location that they can "
"transport to with the use of a Lloyd's Beacon item."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:463
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:6
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There are three plants that can be used to make the three basic potions.  "
"They are poppysnaps, phirna root, and widoweeps berries.  Just mix the "
"crushed flowers, roots, or berries respectively with water to get the "
"potion."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:464
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:7
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Castle Kriegspire was originally built to study the extinct volcano in which"
" it rests, but recent activity from that mountain has chased all humans from"
" the castle.  It hasn't been destroyed yet, but monsters are the only ones "
"that dare live inside it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:465
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:8
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The dragons from Dragonsand have taken advantage of the devils' attacks and "
"have spread out from the desert into the nearby wastelands. They are even "
"rumored to be as north as Kriegspire."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:466
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:9
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Some monsters can be reasoned with.   If you know the charm spell, for "
"instance, you can make even the most ferocious of beasts temporarily "
"friendly.  Remember– you don't have to kill everything you meet.  Sometimes "
"just getting past them is enough."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:467 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:497
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:10
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:40
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Lady Fleise is the Queen of the Merchants, and she has built a huge fortune "
"by controlling shipping prices."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:468
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:11
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Occasionally some coastal towns or slow ships are attacked by pirates.  "
"Fortunately, pirates are rare, but their attacks can affect prices in the "
"towns they plunder."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:469
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:12
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Certain monsters and spells can reduce your body to ashes, making efforts to"
" raise the dead difficult.  We healers call this eradication.  Only special "
"temples and spells can cure eradication."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:470
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:13
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You don't need a powerful spell caster with you for healing.  All the towns "
"and castles have temples with healers.  You can make healing potions, find "
"items with healing spells in them, or even magical fountains or shrines that"
" can heal you."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:471
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:14
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The largest Guild of the Self was founded in Silver Cove."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:472
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:15
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Whenever you have the opportunity, it pays to become an expert or master in "
"any given skill you've been practicing.  Experts and masters enjoy benefits "
"and effects out of the reach of people who just learn the basic skill."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:473
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:16
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It's important to fight creatures challenging to you.  If you fight weak "
"creatures, you don't learn much experience, and if you fight hard creatures,"
" you run the risk of dying.  The creatures at your skill level are the most "
"rewarding to learn from."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:474
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:17
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Always wear armor if you can!  Always!  And spend a little effort to learn "
"to use it or you'll wallow like a pregnant yak in a fight!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:475
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:18
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A man had wandered through not too long ago proclaiming to have knowledge of"
" ancient weapons, the likes of which have not been seen since the Time of "
"Wonders.  We laughed him and his insane ramblings right out of town."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:476
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:19
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"This spell is my personal favorite.  It works best on the strongest and "
"toughest monsters by making them heavier, and smashes lots of important "
"internal organs.  It seems to cut their health in half, and with the strong "
"ones, that can be quite a bit."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:477
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:20
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The greatest magical researcher since the Silence, Twillen's age has finally"
" caught up with him.  The last I heard, he was searching for a way to find "
"his youth again.  I don't think even he can counter the forces of nature."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:478
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:21
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Dark magic makes up one half of the Mirrored Path.  Dark cannot exist "
"without light, nor light without dark.  'Evil' is the word most commonly "
"associated with the school of dark, but that's not true.  A school, like a "
"weapon, isn't good or evil by itself–  it's morality is determined by its "
"use."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:479
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:22
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Although banks in Enroth don't pay interest, they protect your money from "
"theft and loss.  You should consider putting your money in a bank before "
"embarking on any long or dangerous trips."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:480
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:23
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Ahhh, the point of being a merchant!  Gold makes the world move.  Economies "
"bustle with exchange of gold, from markets to farms, to towns, to kingdoms– "
"everywhere!  Even kings spend the lives of their men more readily than they "
"will their gold.  Being a merchant is the way to accumulate wealth, and that"
" wealth gives me a status that most people will never have."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:481
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:24
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There is a small village around Abdul's Desert Resort that sells some of the"
" finest magic equipment I've ever seen.  Heaven knows where they get it, but"
" it sure is nice to know that stuff is available there."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:482
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:25
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Beware of highwaymen plying the roads between towns.  Wise travelers will "
"take advantage of Enroth's many high quality banking establishments to avoid"
" being completely robbed by these parasites."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:483
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:26
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A whole culture of underworld people exists, though it is sometimes "
"difficult to find.  Thieves and criminals have their own organizations and "
"codes, and are surprisingly good at spreading information.  Though you can't"
" always trust them, it's wise to use them as best you can."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:484
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:27
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I've build a few secret doors in my day, and I think I can safely say that "
"some of them are virtually indistinguishable from a plain old wall.  If you "
"have the Wizard Eye spell, you can use it to look at the map it makes for "
"you and logically work out whether or not a section of wall is part of a "
"secret door."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:485
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:28
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Hey!  I'm a legitimate locksmith, not some shady burglar or thief.  I help "
"protect peoples' belongings, not steal them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:486
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:29
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A pipe gives a wise man something to think about and a fool something to "
"stick in his mouth."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:487
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:30
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Speaking of dooming yourself, poor Roland should never have bitten off as "
"much as he did.  I'm sure he met his end courageously, but it was far too "
"early in his life."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:488
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:31
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Don't be careless with the way you pack your goods in your backpack!  A "
"little organization can save a lot of space, and let you carry more.  No "
"one's going to do it for you, you know!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:489
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:32
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Some places it is simply too dangerous to rest.  Never assume you can rest "
"in a difficult area.  Try and save enough strength to be able to retreat to "
"a safer area."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:490
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:33
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You know, it really makes me uncomfortable to have to do business with or "
"hear accounts from criminals.  I know they've stolen money, but what am I to"
" do about that?  Jail is reserved for only the most violent or persistent of"
" criminals.  Bring back Archibald and the good old fashioned execution, "
"that's what I say!  King Roland's too soft, and so is his regent."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:491
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:34
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"One of the best ways to make money is to curb your expenses.  Find the "
"cheapest places to get supplies, healing, and training.  Don't hire people "
"you don't need, don't pay for travel unless you need to, and don't buy items"
" you don't intend to use.  Saving money is as important as making it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:492
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:35
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There's a way to make a powerful potion by mixing common herbs into water "
"and the simple potions that process makes into more complex potions.  I know"
" that if you mix an orange potion with a green potion you'll end up with a "
"white potion of extreme protection.  There's a lot of other combinations you"
" could try, but experimenting is dangerous!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:493
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:36
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I love a well prepared steak, seasoned with a few herbs, and served with "
"onions and mushrooms.  Add some steamed vegetables, maybe a potato, and some"
" good ale… now that's a meal!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:494
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:37
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Now, not a lot of people like to go to the Mire of the Damned, and I'm one "
"of them.  Horses don't belong there, either, and I don't think you'll soon "
"find a stagecoach company willing to take you there.  My advice is to stay "
"away from that place.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:495
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:38
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"In my last visit to Castle Ironfist, Nicolai raved over how much he wanted "
"to visit the circus.  I played a few songs from the circus for him, and he "
"seemed to appreciate the gesture a great deal."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:496
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:39
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It isn't wise to laugh off prophecies, even if, admittedly, most don't come "
"true.  The most important one of our age is the one by Apius Silanus made on"
" his deathbed 800 years ago when he said the dark brother would rise again "
"in the shadow of the light brother's sunset.  That sounds an awful lot like "
"our King Roland and his wicked brother Archibald, doesn't it?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:498
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:41
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Alamos is the home of many researching sorcerers and their magyar guards.  "
"Rumor has it the sorcerers there study summoning spells, but no one is brave"
" enough to go there and ask."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:499
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:42
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you're ever facing a horde of small monsters, try using the Ice Blast "
"spell on them.  It explodes into dozens of tiny shards of ice that bounce "
"around and slice your enemies to ribbons.  Because it will bounce off the "
"walls, it works even better indoors.  Make sure you cast it far away from "
"yourself, or it will hit you, too."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:500
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:43
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you're going to be teleporting around everywhere, it's important to keep "
"good maps to avoid getting lost."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:501
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:44
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Light magic is the strongest magic in the world that doesn't bite you for "
"trying to use it.  Dark magic can work offensive miracles, but often as not "
"there's a price to pay for using it.  Also, many of the most destructive "
"dark magics hurt the caster at the same time it hurts the enemy."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:502
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:45
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Pipe music seems to have a strange effect on rats and children.  At least it"
" does when I use my best pipe.  They follow you everywhere!  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:503
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:46
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I've never made it to Star Island, but I've seen the statues outside.  No "
"one has ever come back from a trip to the island, and I suspect the statues "
"are the transformed people that have made it to the island and discovered "
"some terrible secret there."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:504
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:47
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"For sea battles, there's nothing like a trident for dealing with enemies.  "
"The trident works underwater, or from the surface into the water.  Most "
"weapons can't cut through the water well, but a trident stabs right through "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:505
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:48
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Rumors abound that the council actually guards a cache of equipment from "
"before the Silence.  I don't believe it, though.  Wouldn't the council have "
"used this equipment against the devils, or even in the Succession War if it "
"were true?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:506
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:49
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Here, let me see your palm…<pointing at a line on your hand> Ah.  Well, just"
" as I suspected.  You're going to die.  Soon, I'll warrant."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:507
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:50
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A dagger or knife is the most useful weapon in the world.  You can use it "
"for a variety of tasks, from cooking to carving to lock picking (in a "
"pinch).  Plus, as you become more and more skilled, you can use one in "
"either hand and even strike vital locations on enemies with precise attacks."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:508
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:51
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If ever there was a snake's nest of politics and religion, it was Karigor.  "
"Karigor is a small island southeast of the 'bootleg' that New Sorpigal is "
"situated on.  The twin rival Churches of the Sun and the Moon were founded "
"there, and fought the longest war the world has ever seen until they managed"
" to destroy one another about 200 years ago.  Their artifacts of power are "
"scattered around the world."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:509
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:52
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Temple of Baa is full of insane cultists bent on world domination!  "
"Their evil is everywhere, and they're out to get you and me!  Our only "
"chance of escape is to kill their leader, Wilbur Humphrey, before he poisons"
" the ear of the prince any longer!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:510
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:53
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A bandit that prowls up north, he is notorious for collecting 'protection' "
"from merchants.  He has a good racket, but I'm not sure how long it'll last "
"before someone does him in."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:511
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:54
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Don't tell anyone I said this, but people are saying the Ironfists have lost"
" the Mandate of Heaven.  What else could cause all the storms and floods and"
" disasters?  These are signs of heavenly wrath, mark my words!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:512
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:55
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"With all of the troubles that are going on, I'm certainly glad to be "
"protected by my lord!  Other people might have to worry about their well-"
"being, but all I have to focus on is the work that must be done."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:513
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:56
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Gauntlets are more an armorer's specialty than a tailor's, but I can tell "
"you that the best stuff is available in the armorsmith shops of the far "
"north.  The finest of these magical gauntlets are almost as easy to wear as "
"a soft glove, yet protect every bit as well as the hardest plate gauntlets."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:514
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:57
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"As much as I hate being a lowly laborer, I'd much rather be me than any of "
"the Ironfists.  Troubles seem to follow them like ants at a picnic.  I lead "
"a simple but happy life… better that than to be a miserable noble."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:515
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:58
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There's been a lot of troop movement, these days.  All these soldiers keep "
"walking over my fields!  Now you tell me– what do you think happens when an "
"entire army walks over your crops?  Yes, that's right!  Financial ruin!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:516
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:59
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Fortunately there are a lot of taverns and inns around; they keep me busy "
"making casks for them.  You can find an inn almost anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:517
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:60
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It's tough being a potter these days– there's no reason making it harder on "
"yourself.  Always go to market knowing what prices should be, and make sure "
"you come armed with your wits!  Someone without any merchant skill is likely"
" to get bad bargains."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:518
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:61
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you're planning on staying up north for very long, make sure you pack "
"warm clothes.  It never seems to stop snowing up there."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:519
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:62
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Dragonhide is the best material to use when making any shoe, belt, or boot."
"  It is supple, yet tough and resistant to the elements."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:520
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:63
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"With all the practice I have digging, I should go to the islands in the bay "
"and dig for pirate treasure."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:521
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:64
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Well, with all this bad weather going on, at least the wind is good for me."
"  I have two windmills, and a little wind goes a long way to saving me a lot"
" of money on labor costs!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:522
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:65
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Perhaps I should move to Regna.  They have the largest navy in the world.  I"
" could easily adapt to shipbuilding.  I mean, wood is wood, right?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:523
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:66
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Gems can be worth quite a bit of money, so don't get rid of them or sell "
"them cheap!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:524
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:67
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Why didn't the skeleton cross the road? He didn't have the guts!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:525
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:68
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Tanning is a disgusting job.  That's why I trap instead of tan.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:526
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:69
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I hate to be begging like this, but the injuries I sustained in the "
"Succession War prevent me from doing most labor. "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:527
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:70
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Don't laugh, but I heard that giant flying bloodsuckers are responsible for "
"killing the cows in the New Sorpigal area.  Gods preserve us!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:528
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:71
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Scattered about the lands are shrines.  I wonder what they're dedicated to "
"and who worships at them?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:529
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:72
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I've scribed some spell books for a number of sorcerers, including Albert "
"Newton.  He's my best customer, as a matter of fact.  He sells the most "
"complex spells to the Guilds of Light and Dark based somewhere in the west, "
"probably near Blackshire."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:530
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:73
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"This Church focused on worshipping the heavens.  The conflict between the "
"Churches of the Sun and Moon was pointless and wasteful.  We're all "
"fortunate they're both gone."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:531
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:74
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Better than digging ditches.  Besides, someone has to keep the machinery of "
"state moving!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:532
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:75
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Do I look bored to you?  I'm not, of course.  Acting like you're asleep is "
"an old guard's trick. "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:533
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:78
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You can tell that Archibald's an Ironfist– he has the trademark bad luck.  "
"Not only did his bid for power fail, now he's a statue in the royal library."
"  At least he gets to spend the rest of his days in the castle."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:534
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:77
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"This Mandate of Heaven nonsense really has the potential to start up some "
"serious trouble.  If someone doesn't figure out what is going on with these "
"disasters soon, the kingdom is going to fall apart!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:535
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:76
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you're ever in need of healing and you don't have enough money to pay "
"those sharks at the regular temples, why not visit a Temple of Baa?  They're"
" healing people for free!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:536
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:79
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I wish I was Nicolai!  He's still a kid, but I bet no one tells him what to "
"do!  He can do whatever he wants because he's the king.  Not like me, "
"everyone tells me what to do."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:537
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:3
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Sometimes you can tell that a weapon is heavily enchanted just by looking at"
" it.  If it's heavy and glitters a lot, it's expensive, and probably very "
"powerful."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:538
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:4
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Don't overlook the defensive value of a good shield.  Yeah, I know a two-"
"handed weapon hits a lot harder, but what do you do if you miss, or if that "
"monster just doesn't go down on the first swing?  That's when a good shield "
"comes into play.  It'll save your life one day, mark my words!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:539
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:5
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Statistics show that most items are broken when the wielder or wearer falls "
"unconscious from damage, or where a monster has a particularly bruising blow"
" to deliver.  The single best way to prevent broken items is to just not be "
"knocked unconscious.  Get healed before it's too late."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:540
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:6
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Most items you find will boost or enhance some basic characteristic about "
"you, but a few will have a more complex effect.  It is these that are truly "
"valuable, and their names are usually in the form of 'item of ' as in wand "
"of lightning bolts."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:541
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:7
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There is an island southwest of Enroth where people say is the headquarters "
"of the Temple of Baa.  Why they would pick such a remote location for such a"
" popular religion is beyond me, though."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:542
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:8
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Rumor has it the westernmost parts of the Frozen Highlands are overrun with "
"powerful creatures.  Maybe even dragons!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:543
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:9
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Not anymore it isn't!  Since the devils came, Paradise Valley is a barren "
"wasteland infested with hundreds of devils.  No one goes in there and "
"survives!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:544 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:574
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:10
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:40
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"King Roland keeps his own personal royal yacht, the Queen Catherine, in a "
"lake just west of Castle Ironfist.  She is a mighty ship, capable of going "
"nearly anywhere quickly, but only the king or the regent can give permission"
" for someone to use her."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:545
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:11
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Many small islands fill Bootleg Bay.  I've heard rumors of temples on the "
"islands, and even pirate hideouts!  I've never seen either, but I can "
"imagine the amount of treasure a pirate would have accumulated."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:546
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:12
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It is important to raise someone from the dead as soon as possible, if you "
"intend to do it.  If you take too long, death may require more than one "
"spell to fix.  This can get expensive!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:547
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:13
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It's possible to create more complicated potions by mixing the simple "
"potions together to create compound potions.  Compound potions are stronger "
"than simple potions and have slightly different effects."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:548
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:14
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Simple potions combine to create compound potions.  Orange potions "
"temporarily boost your armor class, green potions temporarily boost your "
"resistances, and purple potions serve as antidotes to any poison."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:549
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:15
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Everyone has a spell book, but many lack the ability to fill it with even "
"the simplest of spells.  If you can somehow get a spell into your spell "
"book, you can cast it as long as you have enough spell power."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:550
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:16
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A cunning woman– it's easy to forget how intelligent she is when dealing "
"with her.  Aside from gaining vast amounts of wealth, she's mastered several"
" skills, and is associated with a few of the druidic orders of the north."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:551
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:17
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Pay attention to the advantages of small, quick weapons.  If you're good "
"enough with them, you can attack twice as often as you could with a larger, "
"heavier weapon."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:552
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:18
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Some warriors prefer to specialize in one weapon above all others.  This "
"training makes them incredible fighters, but it has a few weaknesses.  They "
"may not be able to find an awesome weapon of the type they've specialized "
"in, or they may be fighting against an opponent that is more resistant to "
"their type of attacks.  Specialists are very good, but they shouldn't travel"
" alone."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:553
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:19
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Be sure to use spells of protection when you have them.  They can really "
"reduce the heartache of being reduced to ash by dragon fire or electrocuted "
"by enemy sorcerer lightning attacks."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:554
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:20
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A powerful sorcerer, Agar tried in vain to create powerful creatures as his "
"slaves so that he could conquer Enroth.  His minions were either too stupid "
"to be of use, or too smart to be controlled."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:555
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:21
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Corlagon took Terrax's Crystal to his estate for studying when he began "
"learning the Necromantic arts.  I imagine the crystal is still there."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:556
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:22
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Diplomacy is the skill that makes people feel more favorable towards you.  "
"If you must speak with someone who doesn't seem to like you, make sure that "
"you use your most diplomatic person to do the talking."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:557
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:23
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I wish I knew who Abdul is.  His shops consistently offer low prices– he "
"must be a bandit trying to launder money.  I can't see any other reason to "
"have the low prices he does."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:558
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:24
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I'm certain the devils destroyed the town of Sweet Water!  It was the most "
"northwestern town in Enroth, and certainly one of the most beautiful.  Not "
"many people made it out that way to visit, but now you don't hear anything "
"about the place.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:559
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:25
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There are two major thief guilds in the land.  One, the 'sanctioned' one, "
"can be found in some of the major towns in the kingdom.  The other, guild is"
" called the Shadow Guild.  They are much more violent and cruel than the "
"sanctioned guilds, and I'm sure the king would put them down if he had the "
"time."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:560
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:26
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The lords themselves are too busy to handle most affairs of state, so they "
"have council members that attend the High Council in Free Haven for them.  "
"Each lord has one council member, and these six people make most of the laws"
" of the state, in the names of their respective lords."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:561
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:27
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Plate armor is, of course, the strongest kind of armor available.  There is "
"a legendary suit of armor called Zeus, and it can imbue its wearer with "
"extraordinary strength, but it doesn’t do much for the personality.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:562
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:28
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I've heard rumors that Zoltan Phelps lost a valuable possession to a group "
"of bandits.  If he had taken proper precautions and had used my services, "
"that wouldn't have happened."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:563
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:29
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I know I charge a lot to travel with, but I'm worth it!  If you keep me "
"around, I'll tell you words of wisdom you'll not soon hear from anyone else."
"  For instance, did you know that a fool and his money are soon parted?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:564
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:30
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It's a pity the Temple in Free Haven was destroyed in the fire.  That temple"
" had the most magnificent altar.  The clerics there could raise people from "
"the dead, even from just ashes!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:565
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:31
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The people who hire me often ask me to carry all kinds of junk I know they "
"can do without.  Sorcerers have got to be the worst.  Pipes, tubes, "
"glassware, junk– the works.  Just keep the best stuff with you and sell all "
"that old junk!  But remember that selling to a general store will always get"
" the worst prices."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:566
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:32
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Resting while poisoned or diseased is not advisable.  You stand a good "
"chance of never waking from a rest while under these conditions.  You should"
" get yourself healed of the poison or disease before resting."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:567
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:33
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The 'Imperial Regnan Navy' has been on a taxation spree recently, and this "
"has raised the cost of sea travel and transportation tremendously.  Many "
"businessmen simply cannot afford to pay insurance on their goods any longer."
"  Somebody has to do something about the troublesome Regnans."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:568
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:34
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Due to the recent problems, people aren't spending as much money as they "
"used to.  I'm afraid the economy is going to suffer quite a bit from this, "
"and everyone will soon feel it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:569
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:35
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Wise men are saying they think the Temple of Baa is behind all the disasters"
" that have been happening recently.  I think they're probably right.  The "
"temple offers free healing, but you should think twice before using it– "
"people are suspicious of the temple, and you'll get a bad reputation for "
"having anything to do with them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:570
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:36
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I've heard of fountains with magical waters that are supposed to exist in "
"the lands.  I wish I could find one of these fountains; I'd love to prepare "
"a meal with some magical water."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:571
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:37
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You don't need to worry about this as much if you travel using the "
"stagecoaches, but if you walk, be sure to rest on grass.  It's a lot more "
"comfortable, and your travelling resources won't get used up as fast as if "
"you try to sleep in the middle of the road."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:572
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:38
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I don't understand why there aren't any major Temples of Baa in or around "
"any of the major cities or castles.  For some reason they all seem to be "
"built in more remote places."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:573
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:39
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Most people don't know about it, but the Dragon Towers posted near each of "
"the towns are quite dangerous to students of air.  They're meant to shoot "
"down flying monsters, but they'll also shoot at flying sorcerers.  They shot"
" at me, once, and I'm lucky to be alive to tell this tale!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:575
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:41
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Terrax was Enroth's first arch mage, and a sorcerer of incredible power.  He"
" developed the foundations for elemental magic, and made the first basic "
"discoveries into light and dark magic.  His crystal is said to hold some of "
"the highest magical secrets."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:576
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:42
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Town Portal spell is the single best spell for travelling huge distances"
" in Enroth.  Masters of water have firm control over where they go and when "
"they can cast this spell.  It's expensive to learn, but well worth your "
"while!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:577
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:43
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you can't learn to retreat, Guardian Angel at least provides a means of "
"escape from certain death.  Anytime you explore a dangerous area, it's best "
"to have this spell cast, just in case."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:578
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:44
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Temple of Baa has been giving a bad name to all religion.  People are "
"beginning to think they're behind these disasters, and I'm beginning to "
"agree.  The gods must surely be angry with their disgusting heresies!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:579
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:45
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Can't count on savage beasts to be soothed by music.  That whole story about"
" controlling beasts with music is just a myth.  I have scars to prove it!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:580
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:46
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Castle Darkmoor, in the deepest part of the Mire of the Damned, houses the "
"most powerful undead anywhere in the world.  That's how the rumor goes, "
"anyway.  I've never actually seen the place, much less been inside of it.  "
"I've made it out of the mire alive, though.  Not many people can say that."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:581
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:47
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I know it sounds bad, but the best job I ever had was Imperial Tax Collector"
" for his Highness, Hareck IX.  We collected tax on a lot of ships, and good "
"old Hareck always let us keep some of the booty– er, I mean proceeds.  "
"<sighs> Yep.  Those were the days!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:582
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:48
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The knight's Lord!  Osric's mastered everything there is in combat, from "
"individual fighting to the logistics of siege warfare.  No one is a match "
"for him in a battle!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:583
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:49
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I can see the mark of doom about your face!  It is like a cloud that hangs "
"just above your head, clouding your features and casting a shadow over your "
"future.  Great and terrible adventures await you, my friend!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:584
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:50
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The priests of Baa are nice, even to gypsies.  You can tell a priest of Baa "
"from the decorative cloaks they wear."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:585
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:51
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If someone won't talk to you, and begging doesn’t seem to be working, try a "
"good, hefty bribe.  Gold loosens a tongue faster than charity."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:586
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:52
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Everyone wonders what secrets the ancient pyramid in Dragonsand holds.  "
"Well, I know.  I went there under the protection of the King of the Dragons,"
" and entered the pyramid.  It's the storehouse for all of the dragons' "
"treasure!  It's packed to the brim with gold and artifacts.  Ahh, just the "
"memory of the beauty brings a tear to my eye."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:587
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:53
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Gah!  Nothing has ruined my livelihood more than the banks.  Because it's "
"nearly impossible to break into them, everyone stores all of their valuables"
" there.  I can't find anything decent to take anymore."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:588
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:54
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It's a shame about the king, what with his disappearance and all.  He must "
"have done something to offend heaven to be so unlucky.  I guess he's getting"
" what he deserves."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:589
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:55
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I wish I was a hero with a sword and shield, instead of a peasant with a "
"plow."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:590
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:56
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Erik Applegate is the tailor most famous for working with alchemists to "
"enchant belts.  Applegate has been working at this task for a few decades, "
"now, and you can expect they've turned out some amazing stuff.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:591
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:57
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I ate some poppysnaps once.  They made me so sick I missed a day's work."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:592
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:58
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I hear there's a terrible blight infecting crops and plants in the west.  If"
" it spreads here, I'll be ruined!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:593
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:59
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"With the destruction of Blackwoode and the stand-off in the Timber War, "
"where am I going to get wood to keep making barrels?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:594
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:60
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You can find the shells of all these little animals along the beach and in "
"the rivers when you're looking for good clay.  They must be very old.  "
"There's a lot of shellfish in the Free Haven Harbor.  Oysters, I think.  So "
"many of them, they clutter up all my good clay!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:595
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:61
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Fancy hats and pretty shirts are nice, but if you're going to be in combat "
"you're better off with armor and a helmet."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:596
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:62
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Have you ever heard of the legendary pair of boots called Hermes?  It's said"
" that the boots can boost their wearer's speed to godlike levels.  I'd love "
"to see that someday!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:597
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:63
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I'm not nearly as skilled as some of the people around here.  If I could "
"cast spells, or heal, or fix things, more people would want to hire me.  Who"
" needs ditches dug anymore?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:598
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:64
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"While the storms have been a big help with the windmills, the water mills "
"are suffering from all the cold weather.  Every time the streams freeze up, "
"no work gets done at the water mills."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:599
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:65
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The last Heavenly Forge stopped working about 130 years after the Silence.  "
"No one has ever been able to repair the Forges."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:600
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:66
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"They say that the streets of Kalimar, the capitol city of Karigor, are made "
"of fine jade, and the buildings all use it too.  Sounds beautiful, doesn't "
"it?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:601
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:67
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Did you hear about the orc ventriloquist whose dummy quit to find a new "
"partner?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:602
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:68
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There's lots of ways of laying a trap that's sure to go off when someone "
"opens a box or steps on a certain spot on the ground.  You'd do well to have"
" a little skill in disarming traps if you're going to go adventuring.  Could"
" save your life one day, you know."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:603
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:69
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Have pity on a poor soul and spare a few coins!  The gods will favor you if "
"you do."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:604
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:70
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Ever try sneaking up on a cow in the middle of the night?  They sleep "
"standing up.  You can knock them over by just pushing hard.  Boy, that is "
"one surprised cow when it wakes up!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:605
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:71
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Who's Ivan Seling?  Only the greatest bow craftsman ever!  I wish I had a "
"bow he made.  No one could be a better hunter than I!  Unfortunately, his "
"bows have become very rare since the Timber Wars."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:606
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:72
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Given the lousy selling price of spell scrolls, I would just hold on to them"
" and use them in emergencies.  Often they are scribed at a very high skill "
"level, so you may find their use worthwhile."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:607
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:73
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Roland's death is proof that the Ironfist line has lost the Mandate of "
"Heaven.  It's time Enroth had new rulers!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:608
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:74
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Rubber for my stamps comes from southern Erathia's more tropical climate.  "
"There's a plant that grows there that saves clerks 'round the world a lot of"
" repetitive writing!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:609
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:75
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I wish I had the opportunity to go on Roland's expedition.  Better to take "
"action and fight bravely against the enemy than to stand around and wait for"
" trouble."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:610
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:78
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I can't believe the strange weather we've been having lately.  I think I "
"might just start betting on the weather.  I could probably make a killing!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:611
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:77
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The king's disappearance is a disaster.  I know that it is hard to feel "
"sympathy for the nobility, but an orderly kingdom is in everyone's best "
"interests.  Losing the king doesn't create order, and there is no one who "
"could possibly replace him without so much bloodshed it would make the "
"Succession Wars look like a schoolgirl slap fight!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:612
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:76
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Once you join the Temple of Baa, you'll be issued temple cloaks and be "
"allowed to visit the Superior Temple of Baa located just east of Castle "
"Kriegspire.  Everyone's going to join us sooner or later, so why wait?  The "
"Superior Temple is quite a sight!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:613
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:79
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"My mother told me that if I do bad things, the devils will come and get me!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:614
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:3
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Don't let the name fool you:  Abdul's discount stores offer really great "
"quality for low, low prices.  He also didn't pay me to say that on "
"Thursdays.  Honest."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:615
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:4
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Always have your best merchant do the talking when you buy and sell stuff "
"through merchants.  If they can make a few more gold pieces off an unwary "
"customer, not a one of them will hesitate, believe you me!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:616
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:5
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Many unusual magical effects occur during annual astrological events, such "
"as the two solstices and equinoxes.  Eclipses, midnight, noon, comets; all "
"these things can be magically significant.  The significant dates this year "
"are:  March 20th, June 21st, September 23rd, and December 21st."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:617
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:6
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"In the land of Enroth, the shades of black and white have special magical "
"significance.  If an item or a potion is colored white, it usually means "
"that it provides a powerful beneficial effect without any sort of negative "
"side effect.  If it is black, it provides the most powerful of effects, but "
"with some sort of unpleasant side effect.  Be careful!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:618
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:7
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Everyone has heard of Abdul's chain of discount stores.  Well, he also has "
"an island resort where the old and tired can be rejuvenated for a hefty fee."
"  They say that Abdul himself lives on his resort Island and rarely visits "
"the mainland."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:619
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:8
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Druidic orders flourish in the grasslands near Silver Cove.  These druids "
"will often arrange stone circles to perform ceremonies or worship nature."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:620
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:9
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The mountains that make up the gap that leads to Paradise Valley are called "
"the Sentinels.  Folk tales suggest they protected the valley from evil; now "
"they serve as a warning to anyone foolish enough to want to enter."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:621 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:651
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:10
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:40
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There are many islands that can only be reached with a combination of boat "
"travel and the Walk on Water spell.  Many of them are inhabited by the most "
"horrible of monsters, but often the finest treasures can be found on them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:622
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:11
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Travel by boat isn't instantaneous; it takes time.  Don't forget to factor "
"in your travel times if you're running on a deadline."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:623
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:12
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There once was a temple built by Lord Stone in the city of Free Haven, but "
"it was burned down by vandals a few years ago.  The quality of the altar "
"there was so good that it permitted the priests to raise anyone from the "
"dead, even eradicated bodies."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:624
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:13
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A low level body spell, First Aid is very efficient in terms of its casting "
"cost, but slow.  If you have plenty of time, it's the best way to heal "
"damage."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:625
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:14
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The pinnacle of light spells, Divine Intervention does just that– calls for "
"Eyla, goddess of healing, to intercede on your behalf and heal your group to"
" full life.  Her price, a part of your life-force causing you to age a few "
"years, is sometimes well worth her attention."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:626
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:15
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Training centers are the best way to increase your level, but they can get "
"awfully expensive later on.  Personally, I recommend Abdul's Discount "
"Training centers to avoid excessive training costs."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:627
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:16
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"No teacher in the world can equal the Oracle in Free Haven.  The only catch "
"is that to visit the Oracle, you need to have the unanimous approval of the "
"High Council."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:628
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:17
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"One advantage of the sword and the dagger is that skilled users can wield a "
"blade in their left hands instead of using a shield.  Even a fluff head like"
" yourself should understand why that could help."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:629
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:18
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I know how easy it is for us warriors to scoff at the weak mages out there, "
"but they can make themselves useful at times.  Many of their spells can "
"increase your fighting ability by making you faster, or hit better, or more "
"resistant to damage.  As long as they can pull their own weight, mages make "
"excellent travelling companions."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:630
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:19
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Travelling spells represent the most important class of spells for all "
"magic-using people.  Not only do they let you get to places you couldn't get"
" to without  magic, but they let you visit things like health and magic-"
"boosting fountains in remote areas, and use those abilities in dangerous "
"dungeons and castles where you need them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:631
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:20
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Agar's 'finest' creations, these floating heads have surprising intelligence"
" and great power at their command.  Their gaze is enough to put you to "
"sleep.  Rumors abound of even more powerful eyes that can cause panic or "
"even complete insanity."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:632
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:21
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A few Guilds of the Self exist in the lands.  Combining knowledge of mind, "
"spirit, and body, these guilds offer a more generalized study than any of "
"the individual guilds can offer.  Their knowledge of the individual schools "
"isn't nearly as complete, however."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:633
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:22
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Don't let the name fool you:  Abdul's Discount stores offer really great "
"quality for low, low prices.  He also didn't pay me to say that on "
"Thursdays.  Honest."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:634
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:23
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"In the north, businesses are controlled by a few monopolies that prevent "
"competition by any means necessary, even by extortion.  The Shadow Guild and"
" the Thieves' Guild have already started to clash over rights in areas like "
"Silver Cove and Free Haven."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:635
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:24
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Take my word for it when I say the Mire is a bad place to find yourself at "
"night.  The Necromancer's Guild 'retired' to the swamp after Archibald's "
"defeat in the Succession War, and evidence of their handiwork is walking "
"around the swamp freely."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:636
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:25
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You can avoid a lengthy jail sentence for any crimes you've been committing "
"by receiving forgiveness at the temples.  If you run into a guard before "
"receiving forgiveness for significant crimes, you could be looking at a year"
" in jail, or even longer.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:637
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:26
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Many monsters won't reason with you, no matter how eloquently you phrase "
"your requests.  You need to recognize hopelessly aggressive monsters and be "
"rid of them as fast as possible."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:638
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:27
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Many people don't really care for tinkers because we wander and do odd jobs "
"that guilds would like to charge a lot for.  But you like me, don't you?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:639
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:28
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"With all the troubles that have been going on, business has been great for "
"me.  People have found the need to lock up their possessions to try and "
"protect them from marauders or looters.  It's good to know I can give people"
" at least a small sense of security in these dark times."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:640
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:29
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I bought a treasure map from this treasure map salesman I met awhile ago and"
" it says the dread pirate captain Silveka buried his treasure under a tree "
"on one of the  islands east of Free Haven."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:641
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:30
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Loretta is my kind of person.  She makes her own luck, and it's almost "
"always good.  She's got confidence, and that's something you can't just buy."
"  I'm sure that's the reason she's so successful: a confident, positive "
"outlook."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:642
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:31
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I'm sure you've seen the obelisks scattered around the Kingdom.  They say "
"there's a riddle in them just waiting to be solved that shows where to find "
"a great horde of buried treasure.  No one's ever done it, though.  At least,"
" no one I've ever heard of."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:643
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:32
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Aye, I've worked in Osric's army before, tending camp and preparing food and"
" cataloguing supplies.  He's a fair man, and an excellent leader.  He knows "
"how to keep his troops motivated, let me tell you."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:644
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:33
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There are only three certainties in life:  The first is death.  The second "
"is taxes.  And the third is the fact that you'll hear that joke sooner or "
"later."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:645
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:34
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Banks are a safe place to store money.  Unless you personally own a secure, "
"guarded vault, your best bet is to put your money in a bank.  You don't "
"collect interest on your money, but because the banks don't lend out money, "
"you don't have to worry about losing it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:646
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:35
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"One of the few exports the Islands of Regna have going for them, besides "
"piracy, is sugar, cocoa, and cinnamon.  If it weren't for those, I'd say we "
"should ship the Temple of Baa over to Regna and let them sink all those "
"islands!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:647
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:36
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Different inns charge different amounts for the food they sell, but don't be"
" fooled.  The more expensive food will generally last longer than the "
"cheaper stuff.  It's important to have food that will last when you plan to "
"be out for long periods of time."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:648
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:37
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I can't say I know much about travel over water, but from what I've heard, "
"you can either take a ship to the islands, or Walk on Water to get there.  "
"Ships all have complicated itineraries– be sure to ask the shipping company "
"before you book passage when they do return voyages!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:649
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:38
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It's a shame that Catherine was pulled away to her father's funeral so soon "
"after Roland's death.  That poor woman has suffered too many tragedies too "
"soon.  It's even sadder that she's leaving Nicolai here while she's gone.  "
"He's too young to have to deal with all of this on top of the crises "
"affecting the kingdom."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:650
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:39
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Necromancer's Guild first appeared publicly during Archibald's brief "
"reign 10 years ago.  They were around before that, but they kept themselves "
"secret, knowing people wouldn't appreciate them.  When Roland became king, "
"he outlawed the guild and ordered the leaders arrested.  None of them stayed"
" around long enough for that, though, and now they're nowhere to be found."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:652
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:41
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Dragons are not only adept combatants, they are wily spell casters.  Few "
"people appreciate the dragons' grasp of magic, and many cocky warriors find "
"themselves unprepared for the dragons' true power."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:653
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:42
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Erathia is out of even Town Portal's long range.  That continent is a full "
"six week's worth of sea travel away.  There are a lot of islands and sub-"
"continents between here and there, all of them filled with petty kingdoms "
"and tribes looking to rob travelers of their valuables, their freedom, or "
"their lives."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:654
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:43
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I've seen a few devils in my travels, and they are fierce to behold.  I've "
"had to rescue a few people from devil attacks, and I  was amazed at their "
"coordination and prowess in combat.  They must have excellent training to be"
" that proficient."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:655
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:44
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I fear the Night of Shooting Stars was an omen of the worst kind.  It didn't"
" take long for our good king to disappear after that night, and for the "
"Temple of Baa to arrive, did it?  And all this talk about devils in the "
"west…these are evil omens indeed!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:656
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:45
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Once I was hired by a noble to entertain him and his wife on Star Lake, "
"playing music while they picnicked in a boat. When we approached the south "
"end of the island at the center of the lake, we saw the most hideous beast– "
"a woman with snakes for hair– on the shore of the island.  She took one look"
" at my noble benefactors and they turned to stone before my eyes.  It was "
"all I could do to row away before I joined them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:657
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:46
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Flight spells provide a way to get past mountains and walls and other such "
"obstacles.  There is a limit on how high you can fly with the Fly spell, "
"though.  Some peaks rise too high to pass with magical flying."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:658
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:47
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Hareck IX has got to be the best leader in the world.  Not only is he the "
"only Emperor in the world, he's the only leader I've ever heard of that does"
" common work like the rest of his people.  Like when there's taxes to be "
"collected on shipping, Hareck's right there with the rest of us.  Boarding, "
"fighting, cursing, drinking, whatever.  Hareck's a real down to earth kind "
"of Emperor."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:659
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:48
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Every squire knows that a weapon is of no use broken.  Every warrior should "
"know how to repair his own equipment, or be at the whim of the smiths' "
"schedules.  Knowing how to repair your weapon is part of mastering your "
"weapon."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:660
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:49
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Of all the malicious mischief makers in the world, Necromancers are by far "
"the worst.  Their 'science' is very new, and they know just enough to get "
"themselves and the rest of the world in trouble."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:661
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:50
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Resting revives your body and mind.  Camping gives you a chance to relax, "
"talk, celebrate– to just unwind a little and rest off some of the stress and"
" worry of the remainder of the day.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:662
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:51
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A wise negotiator once said, 'On whether 'tis better to be loved or to be "
"feared, choose both.  But if a choice between the two must be made, choose "
"fear.'– Words to live by, my friend.  Words to live by."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:663
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:52
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Up north, it's not uncommon for wealthy businessmen to preserve their "
"position in the market by hiring thugs to trim their competition.  Trade "
"wars can become quite literally wars.  It's best to not get involved in any "
"merchant disputes."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:664
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:53
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Some of the best perception and lock-picking teachers hang out in Thieves' "
"Guilds."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:665
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:54
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Even if King Roland did something bad to cause heaven to abandon him, I "
"don't suppose that his son Nicolai deserves it.  After all, he's only ten "
"years old.  Maybe heaven will smile upon him and give him heaven's mandate "
"to rule wisely.  That would be nice."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:666
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:55
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I can't leave the towns and castles without some bandit taking away what "
"little money I actually manage to save.  Why can't the guards do something "
"about all the brigands?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:667
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:56
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Indigo from Regna was cut off a decade ago when the king outlawed trade with"
" that pirate kingdom.  I can understand why he did that, but I sure am tired"
" of the indigo shortage.  I can't dye anything blue or purple!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:668
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:57
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"What do you want from me?  I'm just a worker; I'm not here to amuse you."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:669
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:58
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It sure has been raining a lot, lately.  It would be terrible if the clouds "
"ran out of rain and the rivers ran dry because all the water had been used "
"up during these storms.  If the rivers all ran dry, I'd be ruined!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:670
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:59
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Chests and boxes aren't the only things that can hold treasure.  Barrels can"
" also hold valuables, so don't forget to search them, too."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:671
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:60
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Shipping has slowed from Erathia, which is where I get all the paints I need"
" for my work.  That's the land the queen comes from.  I wonder if there's a "
"problem over there?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:672
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:61
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I don't know who makes them, but every Baa priest has a cloak with the "
"symbol of Baa on it.  I wish I had the job of making all those cloaks, I'd "
"be rich!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:673
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:62
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"History is the sound of soft-soled slippers going down the stairs while "
"hobnail boots climb up the stairs."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:674
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:63
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I sure wish I could learn to do something other than dig ditches, but I'm "
"just not bright enough."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:675
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:64
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Flour's been going bad early this year, even though it's properly stored in "
"sealed containers.  I wonder what's going on?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:676
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:65
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Don't forget that you can store things in cabinets.  Chests aren't the only "
"places to keep your treasure."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:677
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:66
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The roads of Enroth are made of flagstones from the hills near Kriegspire.  "
"They were placed long ago by the people who first settled Enroth, and those "
"first roads have never eroded or decayed in any way.  Very odd."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:678
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:67
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What do you call a jittery sorceress? A twitch!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:679
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:68
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Dark days are upon us, mark my words!  Never have I seen so many monsters "
"and so little game."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:680
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:69
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Nothing is worse than trying to beg near Silver Cove.  All the people there "
"are so greedy!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:681
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:70
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Shadow Guild is the best place to find a buyer willing to take stolen "
"cattle.  There's nothing they won't do!  They're great, AND they charge less"
" than the regular Thieves' Guild.  You gotta try them out!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:682
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:71
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"With the lack of animals and all the problems lately, I should probably just"
" become a bounty hunter.  I could probably make a fortune tracking down all "
"the lawbreakers."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:683
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:72
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The most demanding master to have to work for is Osric Temper.  No one else "
"shouts as much, or talks as quickly during a dictation.  I will say this "
"though– of all the Lords, he is the only that seems to be on top of the "
"devil situation we all know is so serious.  Unpleasant to work for to be "
"sure, but he has the interests of the kingdom at heart."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:684
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:73
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Have you spoken with Baa today?  Let me help you come to grips with your "
"problems and show you a better way; it will only take a little of your time."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:685
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:74
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A lot of people complain about taxes, but I just want to say I like them.  "
"How could clerk's offices function without tax money?  How would people get "
"permits and licenses without us?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:686
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:75
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The towers outside the towns shoot at flying creatures that we'd normally "
"have a difficult time handling."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:687
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:78
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Most people don't have confidence in Nicolai.  I'll bet you 3 to 1 odds that"
" he gets thrown out before his next birthday.  What'd ya say?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:688
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:77
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I do hope that the queen returns from her trip to her homeland soon.  Even "
"if she is a foreign queen she will supply some semblance of order to our "
"besieged kingdom."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:689
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:76
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"No one knows where the Supreme Temple of Baa is, but I've heard only full-"
"fledged priests and high temple officials are allowed to visit."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:690
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:79
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Do goblins have names?  Or families?  Why are they evil?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:691
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:3
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The best all around weapon shop in Enroth is the Knight's Paradise, run by "
"Eric Regent.  You can't buy better weapons anywhere else in the kingdom. "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:692
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:4
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You know, metal for arms and armor used to be a lot cheaper before Snergle "
"wrested the dwarven throne away from Rocklin, the old King of the Dwarves.  "
"Sure would be nice if someone fixed Snergle's wagon."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:693
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:5
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Once you are a member of a particular type of magic guild, you won't need to"
" keep buying membership into different branches of the same guild.  A member"
" of the Guild of Fire, for instance, need not buy membership in another Fire"
" Guild in order to take advantage of their services."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:694
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:6
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Albert Newton is the Lord of Mist, and he is truly the patron of all who "
"hold dear the mystical arts.  If you have a question about magic, Mist is "
"where you should look for an answer."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:695
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:7
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Beware travel in the swamps south of Castle Temper.  The undead are said to "
"roam about freely, unafraid of the living or the sun."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:696
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:8
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I never seen one, but I've heard stories of magical portals– doorways– that "
"lead instantly from one part of Enroth to another.  That would take all the "
"fun out of travelling, wouldn't it?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:697
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:9
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Aptly named, Dragonsand is full of both dragons and sand.  I think the most "
"powerful dragons are more than a match for the devils, or the devils would "
"have long ago taken over the desert."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:698 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:728
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:10
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:40
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It is said that one of the islands east of Free Haven hides the buried "
"treasure of Silveka the pirate.  Now, I know these stories are a dime dozen,"
" but I swear this one is true!  If only the map could be found…"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:699
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:11
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Isle of the Hermit is a fairly large volcanic isle in the southwest of "
"Enroth. No one goes there and it's more barren than even the wastelands.  It"
" was named when Lord Terrance made a joke about a hermit living there to get"
" away from it all."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:700
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:12
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"All of the Necromancers in the Kingdom have been banished, happily, except "
"the ones who took their black art too far and became liches.     The worst "
"of those liches, Archibald's former general Lord Corlagon, has taken up "
"residence in the south eastern portion of the Mire of the Damned."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:701
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:13
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It IS possible to combine compound potions with simple or compound potions "
"to try and make complex potions.  Though complex potions are the strongest "
"you can make, the process is dangerous.  Mixing the wrong potions can cause "
"violent reactions and set off dangerous explosions."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:702
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:14
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I know only one formula for a complex potion– the combination of a compound "
"potion with either a simple or compound potion.  Mix a potion of resistance "
"with a potion of cure poison, then take that potion and mix it with a potion"
" of protection, and you end up with a potion of divine cure."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:703
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:15
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Thief and Mercenary Guilds are the places you go to learn all kinds of "
"skills.  Different guilds teach different skills, so if one doesn't have "
"what you're looking for, try the guilds in a different town."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:704
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:16
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Quests aren't anything magical, they're simply opportunities...  "
"Opportunities to learn a great deal or to make a great deal of money.  Try "
"not to pass up the chances you get."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:705
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:17
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Try to equip everyone in your group with a bow, crossbow, or some other "
"ranged weapon.  You can do a lot of damage to an opponent as they approach "
"you, and ranged weapons let you attack flying creatures that otherwise "
"couldn't be hurt."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:706
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:18
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Most warriors like to train in a variety of weapons.  Usually, one weapon is"
" trained higher than the others, but few are ignored.  This provides great "
"flexibility in combat, because you can use the weapon that is most effective"
" against the enemy you face."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:707
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:19
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Some monsters are resistant to nearly all magic spells.  If you run into one"
" of these monsters, don't despair– use your magic to heal your warriors and "
"strengthen their blows."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:708
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:20
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Albert Newton is a brilliant magical researcher, but his research always "
"seems to take a long time to complete.  He certainly knows quite a bit about"
" sorcerers and their magics, however.  If you have any questions about that,"
" he's the person to talk to."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:709
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:21
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I've heard tales of a powerful magical staff that boosts your magical "
"reserves and can strike as swiftly as the wind itself. "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:710
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:22
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"General stores will buy  nearly anything, but give terrible prices.  If a "
"general store is the only store around and you need to sell something fast, "
"go ahead and use it.  But if it can wait, you'll do better selling something"
" to a more specific store."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:711
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:23
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Not all shops are the same!  Some stores offer lowly goods, while shops in "
"other towns have excellent wares for sale.  You'll need to look around and "
"find the good shops for yourself, but keep in mind:  You get what you pay "
"for.  Great equipment never comes cheap."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:712
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:24
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"This foul place is the center of the most serious crimes against nature the "
"Necromancer's Guild has been committing.  My firm scout's advice is to "
"avoid, avoid, avoid!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:713
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:25
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"City councils are always looking for people to take care of local jobs for "
"them.  If you need a little extra cash, try dropping by and asking about "
"work.  There's a good chance they'll have something for you."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:714
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:26
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Your reputation affects how people deal with you.  Most people aren't going "
"to trust you or confide in you if your reputation isn't good.  You'll only "
"find friends from thieves and the like, and do you really want them as "
"friends?  You'll need to help others and follow the laws to bolster your "
"reputation."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:715
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:27
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Try to stay close to chimney sweeps– they're good luck!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:716
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:28
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Apparently there's a new Thieves' Guild called the Shadow Guild that's "
"competing with the established guilds across the lands."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:717
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:29
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I just bought the deed to a bridge spanning the White Forest River.  It's a "
"toll bridge!  Soon I'll be rich as my professional bridge managers make "
"money from the tolls they charge and put it in my bank account!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:718
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:30
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I can never get work in Castle Ironfist.  I don't understand why.  It's "
"almost as though they don't want people crawling around the castle.  Are "
"they hiding something?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:719
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:31
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I travel with all kinds of people, carrying heavy loads from one place to "
"the other.  I tell you though, unless you're powerful, your load will be "
"lightened for you by all the bandits on the roads.  Stay off the roads "
"between cities if you know what's good for you."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:720
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:32
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Many inns are scattered across Enroth, and I believe there are even a few "
"that eke out a meager existence in the western reaches.  These provide the "
"easiest way to get food and the safest rest."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:721
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:33
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Ever notice how the cost of Resurrection at a temple is exactly equal to all"
" the gold you had with you when you died?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:722
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:34
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you find a great piece of equipment for a low price, by all means buy it."
"  You'll be able to sell it later for a profit, and maybe even get some use "
"out of it until then.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:723
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:35
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I've cooked a lot of fish in my day, but never have I cooked one of the "
"deadly eels that infest the waters north of Silver Cove.  I'd love a chance "
"to do it, but not many people tangle with the eels and live.  But, oh, for a"
" taste!  They say the eels are the best delicacy the world has to offer!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:724
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:36
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Never run out of food!  You don't gain any benefit from rest when you have "
"no food, and it's very easy to starve to death in the wilderness if you have"
" no food."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:725
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:37
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Somewhere out there is a set of horseshoes that protect your horses' hooves "
"perfectly, and never lets them get tired!  The places you could go if you "
"had horses with those qualities!  Oh, well.  It's just a legend, most "
"likely."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:726
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:38
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Soon after Archibald's defeat, I was able to peek into the Royal Library "
"after one of my many performances at Castle Ironfist.  Inside, I saw a "
"statue of Archibald in magnificent detail.  He must have had the statue made"
" when he thought he was going to win his insurrection, and Roland's kept it "
"as some sort of memento."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:727
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:39
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Every spell caster knows, or should know, that certain spells and magical "
"effects occur around dawn and dusk.  For instance, no Divine Intervention is"
" possible at any other time."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:729
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:41
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The old Dragon Towers were built to protect the towns from flying creatures,"
" but they'll shoot down anything within their range that's flying."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:730
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:42
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Though the Church of the Moon celebrated the darker side of human nature, it"
" is not to say that good could not come of their evil, just as evil came of "
"the Church of the Sun's good.  During their heyday, the Church managed to "
"create artifacts of great power– the Doomsday Cloaks.  If you ever find one,"
" don't throw it away!  They're all very powerful and valuable."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:731
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:43
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A great spell when running errands, Lloyd's Beacon allows you to set up "
"beacons that you can teleport back to.  Though the beacons don't last "
"forever, with proper planning they last long enough to get the job done."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:732
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:44
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Making a healing potion is a simple matter, if you have ingredients.  All "
"you need are widoweeps berries and a flask with water.  Just mix the berries"
" with the water, and…Voila!  Instant healing potion!  If you don't have any "
"water handy, you can just eat the berries directly, but the effect isn't as "
"strong."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:733
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:45
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Sweet Water was an excellent venue for my music before the Night of Shooting"
" Stars.  Now the road to that town is infested with devils, and they say the"
" town is no more."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:734
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:46
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Isle of the Hermit, named by Lord Terrance for its remoteness, is "
"difficult to travel to because of the turbulent waters south of Enroth."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:735
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:47
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Lots of people would like to invade Regna and take her spices, her metal, "
"and her treasures.  The only thing that's kept Regna free all these years is"
" her attention to metal smithing science and her arms sales to all the "
"countries of the world.  Everyone criticizes Regna for that, but everyone "
"buys Regnan weapons.  Talkin' outta both sides of their mouth, that's what "
"those hypocrites do!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:736
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:48
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I wish I could have been part of Roland's expedition!  There's true bravery–"
" how glorious that troop must have looked, armor and weapons gleaming in the"
" sun.  Better to die valiantly in the battlefield with your lord, then to "
"expire in the night, cold and alone."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:737
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:49
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Astrology is often sneered at, but I tell you it's very real and important."
"  The most significant astrological event recently was that shooting star "
"that fell from the sky out of Sagittarius.  It portends upheaval, disaster, "
"and opportunity for the entire world."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:738
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:50
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Merchants in the northeast aren't above hiring people to make sure that "
"their competition isn't too competitive.  We try to avoid those areas and "
"not get involved with any of the local petty struggles."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:739
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:51
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Listen to the way a person greets you to get an idea how to deal with them, "
"should they prove uncooperative.  You'll find that many people that share "
"similar interests and professions will have the same attitude toward your "
"choice of begging, bribing, or threatening them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:740
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:52
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Don't tell anyone I told you this, but Roland isn't dead.  He simply needed "
"a vacation from all of the pressures of being king, and he's hiding away on "
"Abdul's Resort Isle under a false name."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:741
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:53
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"To keep people like me away from their things, people will often trap their "
"chests. "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:742
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:54
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Weather sure has been strange lately.  Why, last June it snowed!  Snow in "
"June, who'd ever have guessed?  It is an ill omen, snow in summertime."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:743
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:55
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Despite all of my problems, at least the Temple of Baa cares about me and "
"helps me out.  Not like the government we have now."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:744
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:56
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Boots are the cobbler's domain, and I don't know much about them, but I will"
" say that you shouldn't overlook their usefulness.  They can go a long way "
"to adding to your overall personal protection in battle.  Everyone should "
"wear boots."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:745
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:57
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I imagine much of my work in the near future will be digging the graves of "
"the people killed by the devils."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:746
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:58
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I can't even begin to tell you how awful produce prices have been in the "
"market, recently.  I think someone's artificially fixing the prices low!  If"
" this goes on much longer I'll be ruined!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:747
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:59
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Be careful drinking liquids left in barrels; you never know how long it's "
"been sitting there.  You could get sick doing something like that."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:748
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:60
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The wheel spins in the most fascinating ways.  Sometimes I think that if "
"everyone would take a little time out and watch the wheel spin, they would "
"calm down, and be less likely to fight with one another.  But no one will "
"listen to me.  I'm just a lowly potter."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:749
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:61
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It's one thing to make the clothes, but the beauty usually comes from dying "
"the clothes in interesting colors."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:750
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:62
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The fact that our king is missing is awful, but it must be the will of the "
"gods.  How could anything happen that isn't the will of the gods?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:751
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:63
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Lord Temper won't even allow me to become a knight.  He said I wasn't smart "
"enough to follow directions."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:752
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:64
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Mice and rats are a relentless plague upon mankind!  I hear that a keep near"
" New Sorpigal has the biggest rats in the world living in it.  <shuddering>"
"  May I never see such horrors as long as I live!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:753
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:65
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"With all of Blackwoode now destroyed, wood is going to be very scarce in "
"Enroth.  We might see another Timber War starting soon."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:754
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:66
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Tomb of Ethric the Mad is a wonder of fine stone cutting.  My "
"grandfather helped build it.  He says there are some very cleverly concealed"
" secret doors in the Tomb.  Why Ethric would care if a door was secret or "
"not is beyond me, but hey– he was both rich and mad.  I guess he could do "
"what he liked."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:755
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:67
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Why is it goblins have no luck raising chickens? They plant the eggs too "
"deep!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:756
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:68
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The one thing you can say's been good these days is the cold weather.  All "
"the animals have really thick, valuable fur.  Only trouble is finding them."
"  Monsters been eating most of the good fur animals, I think."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:757
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:69
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Just between you and me, I saw a werewolf when I was a werewolf in "
"Blackshire!  I believe all the rumors about their curse."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:758
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:70
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"When cattle rustling gets too hard, I usually spend my time hunting on some "
"Lord's land.  Since most people are afraid to hunt there, those forests "
"haven't been over-hunted.  Recently, though, the animals have been getting "
"scarce.  Could have something to do with the western blight."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:759
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:71
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"In some places it is difficult to hunt for game.  You need to pack more food"
" when you travel in swamps or deserts or snow, for example."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:760
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:72
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Wilbur Humphrey has hired me several times to take notes on disaster reports"
" filtering in from around the kingdom.  I think there's been a sharp "
"increase in calamities since the disappearance of the king."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:761
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:73
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The prince is far too young to manage a kingdom.  Wilbur Humphrey should be "
"ruling the kingdom for himself, not in the name of a child."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:762
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:74
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you ever find yourself in need of work, just stop by the city council's "
"office in one of the large towns.  There's usually a job that needs doing."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:763
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:75
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The rumors of the dynasty collapsing and all the disasters have brought out "
"the worst in humanity.  I need to be even more vigilant than normal to keep "
"the peace."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:764
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:78
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Take it from me, if you want a lucky charm, hang around a chimney sweep.  "
"Sure, their banter can be annoying, but they're the luckiest people I know."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:765
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:77
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I have heard rumors that the recent 'winter during summer' spectacles have "
"been caused by mischievous sorcerers who have learned to meddle with the "
"weather.  I think it's part of a plot to create mass hysteria and open "
"rebellion against the King."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:766
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:76
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The devils people are talking about causing havoc in the west are just "
"misunderstood.  Baa says that they are our friends.  You just have to be "
"respectful and run from them if you see them coming.  They need a lot of "
"personal space, and get angry if they don't get it.  But that's only because"
" they are superior beings.  If we were superior, all this would be easier to"
" understand."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:767
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:79
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I'd love to sail the oceans on a big ship.  I could travel to all the "
"islands and just be free of school and chores and my parents.  That would be"
" wonderful!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:768
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:3
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Word is that the goblins are looking to buy weapons for raids on human "
"towns.  I hear the regent has a sizeable bounty on the heads of any who "
"deliver weapons to those evil little toads."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:769
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:4
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Most any dragon that has a lair is absolutely loaded with gold.  They get it"
" from all the paladins who try to kill them to make a name for themselves."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:770
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:5
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Some of the magic items you find around the world are cursed.  Almost none "
"are pure curses, but many have side effects you won't like much.  You should"
" carefully weigh the side effects against the benefits an item offers before"
" using it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:771
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:6
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Of course you know that spells cast at high noon draw their power directly "
"from the sun.  It is in this way that the mightiest of magicians can afford "
"the power it takes to enchant the magical items you find throughout the land"
" of Enroth."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:772
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:7
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The desert is a land that should be avoided by all but the mightiest "
"sorcerers and knights.  Filled with giants and dragons, nearly all who visit"
" do not return.  Rumor has it that a strange pyramid in the desert holds "
"untold riches and secrets waiting to be unearthed by some brave souls."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:773
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:8
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The pass leading to White Cap and Caste Stromgard has recently been taken by"
" a group of ogres and greedy humans working together."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:774
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:9
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I've heard stories of a horrible curse that has possessed the town. Every "
"time I've visited, however, everything seems normal."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:775 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:805
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:10
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:40
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Although no shipping companies are currently offering the service, Erathia, "
"homeland of Queen Catherine Ironfist, can be reached in a voyage of three "
"weeks or so, depending on the season.  Ain't never been there, but they tell"
" me it's nice."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:776
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:11
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Water walking is nice and all, but it doesn't beat a good ship and a good "
"crew.  Not only are you slower than a ship, you have to worry about the "
"spell wearing off, and you have to worry about sea serpent attacks.  Boats "
"are the best way to travel by water."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:777
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:12
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Resting only really works well in a comfortable place like an inn.  There "
"you can regain lost strength and magic, and heal from most of your wounds.  "
"If you must rest in the wilderness, be sure to have enough food!  Hungry "
"people gain no benefit from rest."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:778
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:13
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Though not as effective as other healing spells, Healing Touch is in the "
"school of spirit, which makes it easier for paladins to learn.  Also, body "
"spells don't work in certain areas, so you will need to use Healing Touch "
"instead of spells like First Aid or Power Cure."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:779
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:14
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Shared Life is an excellent way to keep weaker party members alive when your"
" party is being assaulted with area affect spells.  This spell combined with"
" Power Cure can keep everyone alive when you get in over your head."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:780
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:15
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Many teachers do not want to be flooded by students, so they have moved to "
"remote locations.  You might have to look around quite a bit to find them.  "
"Generally, expert teachers know where their master teachers are."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:781
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:16
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Fame, in many ways, is an accumulation of the experiences you have and how "
"you've managed to share with others.  Quests and brave deeds against "
"monsters can make you famous."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:782
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:17
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Personally, my favorite weapon is the mace.  When you get good at it, you "
"learn to strike at hard parts on your opponent so that it bounces off "
"instead of sinking in.  Saves time.  Anyway, when someone gets hit with a "
"mace, it can stun them so bad that they stop fighting back.  And that's a "
"fine thing."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:783
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:18
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Never underestimate the staff!  Most people associate the staff with a mage,"
" but that's not always the case.  Although you cannot use a shield with a "
"staff, as you become more skilled you'll find that staves are the best "
"defensive weapon around.  Not only that, but they have enough weight to stun"
" people that are hit with it.  It's one of the best all around weapons "
"available."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:784
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:19
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"All of the schools of magic have eleven spells, but only ten can be found in"
" the guilds of darkness.  The missing eleventh spell is called something "
"like Dark Holding or Dark Containment.  No one alive seems to have learned "
"it, and the guilds are very anxious to find it.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:785
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:20
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Summoned by mages to guard areas or items, elementals are beings composed of"
" one of the four primary elemental forces:  air, earth, fire, or water.  "
"Elementals can freely use magics of their element, so be wary if you should "
"battle them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:786
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:21
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Archibald, Roland's brother, mastered many magical arts and accomplished "
"himself as a powerful sorcerer before his demise.  No one seems to know "
"where he is buried, though.  It's as though he disappeared after Roland's "
"ascension to the throne."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:787
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:22
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Skilled merchants run many of the stores in Enroth.  You must be careful "
"when buying and selling to make sure you are not getting ripped off."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:788
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:23
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It's dangerous to carry a lot of money with you.  Banks provide a safe place"
" to store large amounts of money.  Though they don't credit you with "
"interest, you don't have to worry about pickpockets.  That's good enough for"
" me."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:789
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:24
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"In the center of Dragonsand you can find a pyramid marking the Tomb of the "
"Ship, or so they say.  I've scoured the desert and found nothing but dragons"
" and titans to run from.  That doesn't mean it's not there– I had to get out"
" of that desert while the getting was good.  A very dangerous place!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:790
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:25
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I do not like assassins, or men of low character.  And it seems that both "
"types of criminal are spreading through the land like the plague these days."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:791
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:26
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Some creatures you'll run into can be reasoned with if you have a fear spell"
" available.  You can avoid unnecessary and wasteful injury by scaring off "
"your enemies rather than simply fighting with them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:792
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:27
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Sometimes bandits and highwaymen will accept you if they don't think you're "
"'upstanding citizens.'  The weak, however, are always robbed."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:793
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:28
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You must be careful when opening some locks.  Many people don't consider a "
"lock enough of a deterrent, so they will trap their doors or chests to try "
"and frighten off or kill a would-be thief."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:794 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:819
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:29
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:54
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"All of the really bad disasters started happening after the Night of the "
"Shooting Stars two years ago.  Not much has gone right since then, except "
"the Temple of Baa.  They really help people.  They also say that King Roland"
" must have done something awful, 'cause the stars were avenging angels "
"falling from Heaven to punish the wicked."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:795
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:30
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Let me tell you a secret.  There is no such thing as luck.  You make your "
"own luck based on your outlook.  If you expect the worst to happen, it "
"probably will, and you'll have a horrible time.  If, however, you look on "
"the bright side and expect the best, you'll usually find it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:796
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:31
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It's hard to travel through the snow.  Good thing you have people like me "
"around!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:797
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:32
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Resting allows you to approach the new day with vigor and zest.  Resting "
"will heal your wounds and recharge your magic.  Nothing finishes a hard day "
"like a good camp, good dinner, and a good fire."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:798
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:33
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Ever fantasize about discovering a huge horde of treasure?  I do.  They say "
"there are three really big ones:  The first is the knowledge contained in "
"the Royal Library.  The second is the treasure the obelisks lead to.  And "
"the third is in Loretta Fleise's basement!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:799
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:34
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I'm not sure the towns to the west even exist anymore.  Merchants don't "
"travel to there, and no one has come back from those areas yet.  I believe "
"civilization ends at Blackshire, and even the people there are strange at "
"times."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:800
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:35
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It may not seem like a big deal, but I like to supplement my cooking with "
"fresh fruit.  You can find it most places just growing on trees, if you "
"look.  Fruit trees have helped me out when I was hungry and had no money, "
"and they could help you, too."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:801
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:36
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I believe there is a spell that will allow you to create food for yourself "
"out of thin air, but I can't imagine food made from magic tasting very good."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:802
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:37
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I don't suppose you've got any news of Sweet Water, do you?  No one I know "
"has heard anything about the town for a year!  They're a long ways off from "
"here…but a year?  Something must be wrong."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:803
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:38
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I wonder about the council sometimes.  The decisions they've made and some "
"of the laws they've stalled on have really contributed to the chaos around "
"here.  They've stalled any official investigation of Roland's death, and I "
"don't understand why."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:804
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:39
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Practicing meditation may not seem like a big deal at first, but it can be a"
" source of tremendous magical energy to the skilled.  Meditation masters can"
" have many times the spell casting power as their less enlightened brethren."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:806
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:41
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The next best thing to flying, if you fall off of a cliff or similar height;"
" Feather Fall doesn't give you any control but it certainly keeps you alive."
"  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:807
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:42
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The legend of the Crossing is more than a thousand years old, but that "
"doesn't stop people from repeating it from time to time.  The legend says "
"that we all, and that even includes the elves, the dwarfs, and the goblins, "
"came from the same place on a great ship that carried us across the void "
"between the stars."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:808
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:43
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I've heard portals exist that allow transit between two fixed places in "
"Enroth.  Knowledge of these would provide another excellent and fast way to "
"move around the world."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:809
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:44
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The gods oversee our lives and guide us constantly toward heaven and the "
"light.  All you have to do is listen with your heart and do what it tells "
"you to be admitted to heaven.  Have faith.  The gods will help you get "
"there, if you'll listen to them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:810
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:45
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"They say the king was last seen fleeing toward Castle Kriegspire with an "
"army of devils following him.  He never returned.  I think we may have to "
"face up to the possibility that our good king was killed by those monsters."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:811
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:46
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Teleportation is the way to go to minimize travel times.  Of course, you can"
" move around pretty quickly by boat or by horse if you have a skilled person"
" leading the way."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:812
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:47
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I came to Enroth during the time Regnans were invited by King Archibald to "
"bring over a load of weapons to help in his fight against Roland.  When "
"Archibald lost the war, Roland seized all the arms ships and forbade travel "
"to Regna.  I've been stuck here ever since."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:813
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:48
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The simplest piece of a knight's equipment, the shield provides excellent "
"defense for low hindrance and weight.  No warrior should be without a good "
"shield in a fight."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:814
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:49
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The Witches' Assembly of 638 was the greatest gathering of sorcerers and "
"alchemists ever.  Since then, the popularity of the magical arts has "
"declined, and persecution of groups like ours…er, theirs– has grown quite a "
"bit.  It really is quite awful."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:815
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:50
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Merchants are businessmen first and foremost.  They will always try to buy "
"low and sell high.  Don't be too upset with them; they need to make a "
"living, too.  The way to get the best prices, both when buying and selling, "
"is to try different markets."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:816
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:51
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you've determined that begging and bribing are of no use, and you simply "
"must speak with a person, then the thinly veiled threat must be issued.  But"
" remember to use this option sparingly, since only the best diplomats can "
"stop the damage you'll do to your reputation if threats become your habit."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:817
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:52
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Nicolai has commissioned a bridge to be built from New Sorpigal to Mist.  "
"I'm working for him by offering affluent members of society a chance at "
"charter membership of the Nicolai Ironfist Bridge Fellowship.  The basic "
"membership gets your name on a flagstone of the bridge and costs 50,000 "
"gold– a small price to pay for immortality.  Are you interested?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:818
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:53
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Fetzil, the Prince of Thieves lieutenant, is smart; he knows enough to hide "
"out when things get hot.  He's not an easy person to catch."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:820
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:55
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I hate taxes!  Why should we pay taxes anyway?  It's bad enough I have to "
"spend my life working for other people; I need to pay them for the 'honor'?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:821
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:56
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Cotton is found in Karigor, the island home of the Church of the Sun and the"
" Church of the Moon.  It doesn't grow well anywhere else, and it's difficult"
" to pick and seed, but it makes for wonderful soft clothes, if you can "
"afford it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:822
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:57
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If I could actually use a weapon, I'd probably be better off joining a "
"bandit group.  I bet they lead an easy life."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:823
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:58
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Sure's been hard to get help recently.  What is a good farmer to do if he "
"can't find strong workers during harvest times?  Go into bankruptcy and "
"ruin, that's what!  Oh, woe is me!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:824
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:59
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I'd love to hear what the Oracle would say about the devils, the Temple of "
"Baa, and Prince Nicolai.  Why won't the council consult the Oracle?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:825
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:60
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Change is in the air and on the wind.  You can smell it and feel it.  "
"Something big's going to happen soon.  I can always tell."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:826
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:61
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Warm clothes won't help you resist the chill of Castle Darkmoor.  The undead"
" there steal the warmth from your body with their touch."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:827
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:62
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The blight that's afflicting western crops and animals is slowly spreading "
"east.  Cows are affected first, and this is causing a very serious leather "
"shortage.  You can expect the price of boots and belts and other leather "
"goods to be increasing!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:828
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:63
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This isn't the best job in the world, but at least the work is steady."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:829
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:64
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Taxes have been good under this King.  Archibald was terrible, much worse "
"than his father.  I thought I would be ruined by Archibald's cruel taxes.  "
"May he nor his like never hold the throne again!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:830
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:65
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Let me tell you, some bookshelves or desks or other furniture can be crafted"
" to conceal a secret passage.  You can walk through a room and never realize"
" there were two or three other hidden exits."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:831
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:66
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you ever take a trip near Star Lake, be sure to check out the beautiful "
"statues on the island in the center of the lake.  They are so life-like "
"they're breathtaking!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:832
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:67
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What is big and red and eats rocks? A big red rock eater!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:833
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:68
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Come to think of it, the animals all started to go away when the stories of "
"the devils in the West started cropping up.  Yep.  That's probably it.  "
"Pesky critters!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:834
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:69
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'm so pitiful, the bandits that prowl the roads even laugh at me!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:835
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:70
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you think your reputation is getting too bad for people to tolerate you, "
"you should check yourself into a temple and start donating, my friend.  The "
"temple will spread word of your generosity far and wide, and people will "
"think better of you for it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:836
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:71
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you're going to hunt anything, you'll need a bow.  I don't think you are "
"fast enough to chase a deer down with your sword."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:837
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:72
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"When I was much younger, I had a chance to see the ruined library of the "
"Church of the Moon at Karigor.  It was made entirely of jade and marble, and"
" once contained the wisdom of the ages within its hallowed halls. If ever "
"you have a chance to visit, take it!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:838
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:73
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The main Temple of Baa is just northwest of Blackshire.  Only members of Baa"
" are allowed inside."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:839
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:74
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The High Council isn't just an ordinary city council– they are the body that"
" represents the lords of the land.  They vote on important matters of state "
"that need to be taken before the king.  They also control access to the "
"Oracle."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:840
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:75
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It is important for guards to be patient.  We can't go out and look for "
"trouble; we need to wait for trouble to find us."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:841
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:78
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The poor queen has lost both her father and her husband.  Hopefully, nothing"
" will happen to Nicolai. "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:842
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:77
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I'm wondering if something foul indeed fell from the sky that Night two "
"years ago.  I am not, however, of the opinion that it was an avenging angel!"
"  More like a devil, if you ask me!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:843
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:76
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'm fine!  Why do you ask?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:844
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:79
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Why do grown-ups always have to fight?  Why can't people just get along?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:845
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:3
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"What're ya gallivanting' around here for on a Sunday?  It's a day of rest, "
"kid, REST, I say!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:846
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:4
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There are two kinds of magic armor– armor that increases your protection, "
"and armor that is lighter and easier to wear.  A few rare kinds of armor "
"have both of those properties."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:847
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:5
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"When a wand runs out of charges, you've lost the value of the wand.  They "
"can never be recharged, but it's usually possible to find a sucker to buy "
"the wand at full price  just before the charges run out."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:848
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:6
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Combining potions in the right proportions can achieve formulas that do very"
" unusual things.  The Guild of Alchemists closely guards the secrets of "
"which potions have which effects."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:849
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:7
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I don't have much taste for civilization, but you can rest assured that more"
" goods and services will be available on the east coast of Enroth than "
"anywhere else– particularly Free Haven."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:850
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:8
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Horses provide an excellent means of travelling if you can afford the cost."
"  All of the towns and castles  on the mainland have stables where you can "
"hire horses."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:851
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:9
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Mages are so lazy, they've formulated several spells to transport people "
"instantly from place to place.  These spells are good, but there's nothing "
"like a REAL journey."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:852 mmmerge/Data/Text
#: localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:882
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:10
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:40
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I've heard there are sorcerers for hire who can cast the Walk on Water spell"
" if you can't do it yourself.  They charge a lot, though."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:853
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:11
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You need to be careful when planning your boat travels.  Certain areas are "
"too dangerous to sail to during parts of the year."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:854
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:12
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It is important to get treatment for diseases and poisons.  The longer they "
"go untreated, the harder they are to cure.  Getting poisoned or diseased "
"more than once worsens your situation."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:855
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:13
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The highest level spell in the school of body, Power Cure is an effective "
"way to heal the entire party quickly.  One Power Cure heals more damage "
"faster than 4 smaller healing spells."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:856
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:14
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"You generally have more hit points than spell points, so it is often faster "
"to heal yourself as best as possible with magic, then rest.  You can cut "
"down on your resting times quite a bit this way."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:857
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:15
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"As your level of experience increases, so does the amount of experience you "
"need to improve.  You'll get more benefit from a magical effect or reward "
"that increases your level directly later in your life because of this rule."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:858
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:16
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Prince Nicolai shows incredible perception and creativity for his young age,"
" much like his father did.  I don't think people give him enough credit– "
"they're more concerned with his age than his ability."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:859
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:17
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It pays to know how to use two or three different kinds of weapons, kid.  "
"That way you can change tactics in battle if an opponent isn't getting hurt "
"by your favorite fish gutter, if ya know what I mean!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:860
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:18
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Osric is not only a master warrior, but an ingenious general.  I'm glad to "
"see that he's not taking the recent attacks by the devils lightly.  He's "
"already working on ways to fight back, but the situation looks pretty grim."
"  If anyone can come up with a way to fight them, however, it's Osric."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:861
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:19
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If you're facing an opponent that can't be put down with direct damage "
"spells, try a mental attack spell, or something that freezes them in place."
"  This can often give the warriors in your group time to pound the enemy "
"into the ground while distracted by your spell."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:862
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:20
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Gharik attempted to recreate some of the weapons from the Time of Wonders in"
" his forge.  He was never successful, but a number of his experiments "
"provided useful information for enchanting weapons and summoning creatures."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:863
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:21
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"A few Guilds of the Elements exist.  Though their knowledge of the "
"individual elements isn't as pervasive as the more specialized guilds, they "
"are an excellent resource to broaden your knowledge of all the elements."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:864
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:22
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The essence of life!  Gold oils the squeaking wheel, silences the witness, "
"or loosens his tongue.  Gold puts food on the table and wood in the fire.  "
"How I love thee, O mighty gold.  Never run out of gold, my friend.  Never!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:865
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:23
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The most important part of being a merchant can't be taught.  You need to "
"learn to notice a good buy when you see one, and make the good deals when "
"you can.  If you pick up something for cheap in one town, there's a good "
"chance you can sell it somewhere else for a profit."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:866
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:24
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I traveled to the lands west of Blackshire recently, and what I saw chilled "
"my blood.  Devils running about a ruined, blighted landscape, killing any "
"humans they ran across.  Something is terribly wrong.  I just don't know why"
" someone isn't doing something about it!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:867
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:25
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Compared to many countries, Enroth is a very tolerant kingdom.  Nonetheless,"
" you can end up in jail if you commit enough crimes and are foolish enough "
"to show your face to a guard.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:868
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:26
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Diplomacy is the key to negotiation, and negotiation is the key to many "
"closed doors in the world.  You must be able to sip champagne with the "
"highest lords and guzzle ale with the lowest scum if you want to succeed."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:869
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:27
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Find a penny, pick it up, all the day you'll have good luck!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:870
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:28
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Most of the great treasure you'll find will be locked away in a chest or "
"box.  It only makes sense to protect your valuables."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:871
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:29
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It is better to talk and let them think you a fool than to keep silent and "
"prove it!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:872
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:30
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Poor Eric's temper matches the weather in his kingdom.  Seeing a smile on "
"his face is about as rare as seeing the sun in White Cap.  He's got the "
"wrong way of looking at things, ol' Eric does."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:873
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:31
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Lady Fleise is the most difficult mistress to work for in all Enroth, you "
"can be sure of that!  Penny pinching, heart of stone she has!  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:874
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:32
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Different terrains are easier to forage and hunt in.  You don't need to use "
"quite as much food in grasslands, for example, as you do in the desert.  "
"Keep this in mind when you choose a place to camp."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:875
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:33
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Times are tough, and the banks have stopped giving interest payments on "
"deposits recently.  Don't expect anything but security when you put your "
"money in the bank– interest is a thing of the past!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:876
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:34
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Loretta's managed to make money by creating and exploiting her lead position"
" in the shipping industry.  She's able to manipulate shipping prices all "
"over the kingdom which brings in quite a bit of money.  I only wish I "
"handled her accounts."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:877
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:35
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Better and fresher food that keeps longer is also more expensive.  People "
"out west have figured out the trick of making food that keeps for a long "
"time."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:878
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:36
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Herbs can be used to create magical potions.  I don't know the procedure, "
"but I know it's possible.  I wonder how those taste?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:879
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:37
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Although it can be expensive, travel using the stables is faster than most "
"any other way, excepting magic, and not many people can do that!  If you're "
"broke, you'll have to hoof it yourself, but don't forget the food cost of "
"travelling by foot!  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:880
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:38
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I love to perform!  I love to travel!  There is no life like that of a bard."
"  The best gossip, the best food, and, most importantly, the best drink "
"available… why would I ever want to be anything else?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:881
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:39
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Though you can't hear it, the stars and the planets sing as they travel "
"through the sky.  It is the Music of the Spheres– the grandest symphony in "
"the universe!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:883
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:41
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Flying is certainly easier than walking.  Safer, for the most part, too.  "
"The only problem is that the Fly spell continually drains your power, so you"
" need to plan your flight trips carefully so the spell doesn't run out."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:884
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:42
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Water walking– my specialty– permits you to walk across most bodies of water"
" as though you were on dry land.  You have to be careful, though, or the "
"spell will run out while you're still over the water.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:885
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:43
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I've had to rescue a number of doomed expeditions, and let me tell you the "
"one thing I've learned.  If you go somewhere that you don't think you can "
"handle, RETREAT.  No one will think less of you for it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:886
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:44
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The magics of mind, body, and spirit are the magics of the soul and the "
"self.  To improve one's understanding of them is to improve one's standing "
"with the gods.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:887
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:45
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Many people have contempt for the simple music of a travelling minstrel, but"
" it is the work of a lifetime to get good at what I do."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:888
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:46
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Many areas with magical powers are scattered around the world.  Most often, "
"they are in out of the way locations.  It's to your best benefit to try and "
"discover and use as many of these as you can."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:889
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:47
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"People say bad things about my homeland of Regna all the time, but they "
"don't know what they're talking about.  Never will you find a more fun "
"loving, happy people than on Regna, nor a more fiercely independent people."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:890
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:48
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The best way to learn is to make sure to fight challenging opponents.  You "
"don't grow by picking on things weaker than yourself.  The true path to "
"glory leads through winning tougher and tougher battles."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:891
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:49
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There is a mystical deck of tarot cards some claim to have seen.  No person "
"ever sees the deck twice.  To draw from the deck is to draw a new hand in "
"the game of life."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:892
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:50
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Most of the dangerous areas left in the world are found to the west.  "
"Paradise Valley and Dragonsand are the most notable, though the western "
"parts of the Frozen Highlands and the Mire of the Damned are difficult as "
"well.  As a general rule, the farther west, the more difficult."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:893
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:51
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I can't stress the importance of diplomacy enough.  A good diplomat can "
"excuse any action, no matter how foul. "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:894
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:52
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Devils!  Bah!  They're nothing more than illusions created by mages hiding "
"vast treasure somewhere in Paradise Valley.  I know a few of those sorcerers"
" personally, you see.  This ring I'm wearing was a gift from one of them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:895
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:53
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Some people are born to trade, or negotiate, or fight, or study.  I'm born "
"to steal, and I'm pretty good at it.  Times are a lot harder now because of "
"all the calamities; it's hard to find things worth stealing anymore– people "
"are way too careful with what they have."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:896
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:54
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Thank God for Sundays!  If I had to work every day I think I would revolt "
"against my noble oppressors and replace them with a capitalist-bourgeoisie "
"run quasi-democratic society where I would still have to work long hours for"
" little pay."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:897
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:55
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I wonder what life was like before the Silence with a governor in charge of "
"everything?  It couldn't have been very good, or there wouldn't have been a "
"rebellion."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:898
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:56
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There are three styles of hats popular these days, ranging from the cloth "
"hat to the fancy, expensive sort made by the highest quality tailors.  "
"Wizards like to enchant quality hats because they're lighter than helms and "
"don't block your vision.  Also, a certain kind of conical hat seems easier "
"to enchant than others."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:899
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:57
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Before the Silence was the Time of Wonders.  Magical creations handled all "
"the hard labor– I wish I had one to do my chores."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:900
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:58
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"All are equal before the majesty of the law:  Rich man as well as poor is "
"prohibited from sleeping under bridges, stealing bread and begging for "
"change.  –Voltaire"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:901
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:59
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"It's easier to let a barrel roll down hill than to push it up.  Sometimes "
"it's better to just go with the flow."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:902
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:60
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Not all clay is created equal.  The best clay can be found in the bed of the"
" rivers and streams flowing past Free Haven."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:903
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:61
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Some articles of clothing have been enchanted.  It will benefit you to wear "
"these types of magic clothes."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:904
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:62
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Everyone should wear shoes, not just nobles and rich people!  What are you "
"going to do if you hurt your feet?  How are you going to keep working?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:905
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:63
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"If I was smart, do ya think I'd be digging ditches for a living?  Be "
"serious, please."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:906
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:64
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Grindstones are so hard to make and find, it's a wonder anyone ever becomes "
"a miller.  I hear that Karigor has a great rock quarry that turns things "
"like millstones out by the hundreds.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:907
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:65
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Can you imagine the Elves starting a war over deforestation?  Where do you "
"get wood if not from trees?  How am I supposed to make a living if I don't "
"have lumber to shape and build with?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:908
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:66
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Churches and kings seem to spend a lot of time thinking about paving stones "
"and whatnot.  If it weren't for them, I would hardly have any work at all."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:909
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:67
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Why are there only twenty hours in a goblin day? Ever see a goblin with "
"twenty-four fingers and toes?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:910
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:68
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Used to be plenty of game out west.  Not so much, these days. Maybe it has "
"something to do with the blight that's been killing the plants in Pleasant "
"Valley."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:911
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:69
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Most people have too many problems of their own to help out a poor beggar "
"like me, but the priests of the Temple of Baa always seem to have time and "
"money or food for me.  I'm very grateful to them for helping me."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:912
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:70
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"The blight everyone's been talking about has been killing all the cows!  Now"
" tell me.  How's a soul supposed to make a living rustling cattle when "
"there's no cattle to rustle?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:913
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:71
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Mogreds are extinct in Enroth, and almost extinct in Karigor.  They were "
"over-hunted because of how valuable their horns are for enchanting."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:914
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:72
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"There's a paper shortage that's come up recently, and I can tell you, my "
"clients do NOT like it.  It's amazing to hear some wealthy noble like "
"Loretta Fleise complain about the cost of paper.  She probably has the "
"largest pile of gold in the kingdom, perhaps even the world, and still she "
"complains."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:915
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:73
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Based on worshipping nature and the world around us, this church cared less "
"about the people and more about its selfish goals.  "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:916
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:74
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I could certainly use a holiday.  How many clerks do you know of that work "
"every day of the year?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:917
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:75
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I know most people don't feel our job is important.  With the events "
"recently, however, it's extremely important for us to keep order.  We will "
"be as vigilant as ever!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:918
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:78
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I hope your luck is better than mine.  I've lost a lot of money on sure bets"
" recently.  I think the bad luck of the Ironfists is rubbing off on me."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:919
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:77
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I hate Sundays!  It is ever so hard to get good help to work on Sunday.  "
"Like it's different than any other day!  Humph."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:920
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:76
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Baa changed my life for the better!  Surrender your will to Baa, and you "
"will forever be free of doubt and pain!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNews.txt.py:921
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/PROFTEXT.txt.py:79
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"I can't wait for the Circus of the Sun to get here.  I've been good all "
"year, so hopefully my parents will take me to see it!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNewsTopics.txt.py:2
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ooops text"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNewsTopics.txt.py:3
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Peasants on main island of Dagger Wound before the pirate outpost is "
"defeated"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNewsTopics.txt.py:4
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Peasants on main island of Dagger Wound after the pirate outpost is defeated"
" (Questbit 6)"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNewsTopics.txt.py:5
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Peasants on smaller islands before teleporters are fixed"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNewsTopics.txt.py:6
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Peasants on smaller islands after teleporters are fixed (questbit 2)"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNewsTopics.txt.py:7
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Pirates on Dagger Wound Island"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNewsTopics.txt.py:8
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Wolves"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNewsTopics.txt.py:9
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Peasants in Ravenshore city"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNewsTopics.txt.py:10
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Wererats"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNewsTopics.txt.py:11
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid ""
"Were-rats in Smugglers Cove after Fellmoon's letter has been delivered "
"(Questbit 4).  Rats in Dungeo"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNewsTopics.txt.py:12
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All Peasants after end game"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNewsTopics.txt.py:13
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Lizardman Lookouts/cannons"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCNewsTopics.txt.py:14
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Lizardmen Warriors"
