msgstr "Hacha de asta pesada"

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:32
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A stronger version of the basic Poleax, this weapon is frequently used by "
"city guards and other fighters who don't expect to do battle in large, "
"coordinated groups (like armies)."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:33
msgctxt "items"
msgid "Grand Poleax"
msgstr "Gran hacha de asta"

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:38
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A smithy symbol and date stamp indicate this spear was made in the magical "
"forges of Governor Padish 12 years before the Silence (+1D9 if used two-"
"handed)."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:41
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A small stamp on the blade of this weapon indicates it was constructed in "
"the famous Mekorig Foundry by the master himself, Mekorig the Blind.  You "
"would be hard pressed to find a finer Halberd anywhere in the world (+1D6 if"
" used two-handed)."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:74
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"Chain mail is an armor formed of small, interlocking loops of metal.  This "
"suit is low quality:  the metal used is plain iron, there are only two "
"layers of rings, and it is heavy and stiff for its size."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:75
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A superior suit of chain mail, the metal used in this suit is steel, and the"
" former owner was careful to keep the suit well oiled and free of rust."
msgstr ""

#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/ITEMS.TXT.py:78
msgctxt "items"
msgid ""
"A very rare suit of armor turned out by the Heavenly Forges of Governor "
"Padish before the Silence.  The armor was originally worn strictly by the "
"Governor and his highest military officers as a badge of office.  It is not "
"just for show; this chain mail is lighter, stronger, and more supple than "
"any other chain in the world."
msgstr ""

